03` error with the request id.\n3. **Read-only** — `cli/src/index.ts:1213-1222` (inside `serve-mcp`): `readOnly` now comes from `buildConfig(options)`. An empty HOME with no model still starts (every test server runs that way).\n4. **Docs** — `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md:136-144` rewritten with the four additions; line 128 now names `REDACTED`. `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` is unchanged (still true).\n\n## Tests added (`cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts`)\n- `:293` \"SIGTERM to the server stops a verifier that ignores SIGTERM and removes the scratch trees before the server exits\". With the handlers removed it fails (runs to its 180 s limit).\n- `:336` a `REDACTED` case in the refusals test.\n\n## Results\n- `mcp_verify`: 7 pass, 0 fail, three runs in a row.\n- `verify_service`: 10/0. `mcp.test.ts`: 4/0.\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `check_invariants.mjs` exits 0.\n\n## Caveats\n- If `buildConfig` throws, the server still starts and `nexus_verify` is refused as read-only, with a stderr notice; exiting 2 there would have broken startup for existing users with an unrelated config error.\n- The SIGKILL stage is not exercised by any test: under bubblewrap the sandbox dies on SIGTERM even when the verifier traps it, so the test exits in about 7 s on the graceful path.\n- The catch at `mcp.ts:969` has no test.\n- Node 22 was not run.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>245902</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>770001</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
