{"parentUuid":"27223e21-4778-4f83-83b8-336dfbc5e7e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLXAoaZuRGWApDgX1pXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3392,"cache_read_input_tokens":437733,"output_tokens":2849,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":495},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3392,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2849,"cache_read_input_tokens":437733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3392},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5330,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLXAo92VfK3i97Tef4uM","requestRef":"34ab0f1e-a59a-4781-9bbb-b3bda007e9e9","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"aeae4530-dc51-4533-8317-63f58ab1b542","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:51:21.403Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"aeae4530-dc51-4533-8317-63f58ab1b542","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLXAoaZuRGWApDgX1pXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q2k3p4nwPXqF1FbiAimv9S","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aa6055acd1b6e26f5","summary":"Fix review findings in VR-2 ACP half","message":"More follow-up work in /home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2 (branch v1/vr2-verify-for-clients, HEAD f25030a3; start with `git status` and `git log --oneline -5`; do not commit or push; same working rules as before). Another agent added the ACP half of VR-2 in commit fc63f747: an ACP extension method `_nexus/verify` in `cli/src/acp_stdio.ts` (+ `cli/src/acp/{types,validate,mapping}.ts`, schema `docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v2.schema.json` generated by `cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs`, ledger `docs/protocol/ACP_ADAPTER_VERSIONS.json`, tests `cli/test/acp_stdio.test.ts` / `acp_validate.test.ts` / `acp_schema.test.ts`, evidence `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md`, docs `docs/ACP.md`). It uses your `VerifyService`. Read that commit first (`git show fc63f747 -- cli/src cli/test`). An independent review accepted it with follow-ups. Fix these, with tests, and report (under 350 words):\n\n1. Id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` must return TURN receipts only (the plan's decision 7: existing clients see no change). Today `latestReceipts` in the receipt handler (acp_stdio.ts near line 353) mixes verification receipts in, and the test at `cli/test/acp_stdio.test.ts` ~line 118 asserts that. Keep verification receipts readable only by explicit id, bound to the session. Update the test to assert: after a `_nexus/verify`, id-less get still returns the last TURN receipt (or the existing \"not available\" error when there is none), and get-by-id returns the verification receipt.\n\n2. Base pin per workspace, not per session. Today the base is pinned in `startSession` for every new/loaded session (~line 229), so a client can commit weakened tests, open a NEW session on the same directory, and be judged against a base that already contains them. Pin once per canonical workspace path for the lifetime of the `nexus acp` process: the first session on a directory pins `HEAD`; every later session (new or load) on that same canonical directory reuses that pin. Test (fake or real service as the existing tests do): session A on dir D pins B0; commit a change in D; session B on D still reports/uses B0 (assert via what the verify request passes to the service or the receipt's base). Make sure the map cannot grow without bound from client-chosen cwds (cap it, e.g. to a small multiple of ACP_MAX_SESSIONS with refusal of `_nexus/verify` for an unpinned workspace beyond the cap — never silently re-pin or evict a pin).\n\n3. The verify result summary must name what was covered: add the workspace (canonical session cwd) and the pinned base commit to the `_nexus/verify` result (the receipt already has `workspace` and `base_pinned_at`), update types, validation/mapping, regenerate the v2 schema with the generator (`node cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs` — check its `--check` mode passes afterwards; v1 schema must stay byte-identical) and adjust `acp_schema.test.ts` / examples if they pin the shape.\n\n4. Tests for the interlocks, which a mutation showed are untested: `_nexus/verify` while a prompt is running on that session is refused and nothing runs; `_nexus/verify` while the session is `stopping` is refused; `session/prompt` while a verification is running is refused; `_nexus/verify` in read-only mode (config `approvalMode: \"read-only\"` / `readOnly`) is refused with no receipt; cross-session receipt read uses a SECOND REAL ACTIVE session on the same connection (today's test at ~line 125 uses an id that is not active) and must fail. Confirm by mutation that removing the verify-during-prompt check fails a test.\n\n5. Shutdown bound: `ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS` (10 s) equals the verify kill grace, so on a signal `process.exit` can fire before the worker has removed its scratch trees. While a verification is running, the signal deadline must be at least the verify kill grace + 5 s (mirror what `McpServer` does). Look at how the stop/`close()` path in `runAcpStdio` is written now (it was changed by commits \"fix(acp): bound shutdown after a signal\" and \"fix(acp): keep shutdown deadline referenced\"); keep its semantics, only lengthen the bound when a verification is in flight. A test is welcome if cheap; otherwise say it is untested.\n\n6. `_meta` on `_nexus/verify`: either reject it like any other extra member, or keep accepting it and say in `docs/ACP.md` that it is ignored and reaches nothing. Pick whichever matches how the adapter treats `_meta` on its other methods (check `cli/src/acp/validate.ts`) and state which.\n\n7. Docs, honestly: in `docs/ACP.md` (the `_nexus/verify` section) and `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md`: (a) the client chooses the directory a session works in, so a verification covers that directory; the operator's verifier command and deliverable list are fixed at start-up but are applied to the session's directory (check `cli/src/config.ts` ~529 and the worker for how deliverables resolve, and describe it exactly); the result and receipt name the workspace and base so a reader can see what was covered; (b) the base is pinned per workspace for the life of the process (after change 2), so commits made before the first session on that directory are the baseline, and restarting `nexus acp` re-pins; (c) the same-user limit already described in `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` applies. In the evidence doc, replace any test-count claim you cannot reproduce with the counts from your own run at the current head, and keep its statement about hosted CI truthful (say CI results are on the PR rather than claiming none ran).\n\nThen run, one at a time with a throwaway HOME: `acp_stdio`, `acp_validate`, `acp_schema`, `acp_mapping`, `acp_review_fixes`, `acp_client_conformance`, `verify_service`; `tsc --noEmit`; `node cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs --check` (or whatever the check invocation is); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Run `acp_stdio` three times in a row. Report file:line per change, tests added, pass/fail counts, the mutation result, and anything not done or untested.","type":"message","recipient":"aa6055acd1b6e26f5","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"More follow-up work in /home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2 (b…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3392,"cache_read_input_tokens":437733,"output_tokens":2849,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":495},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3392,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2849,"cache_read_input_tokens":437733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3392},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":22825,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q2k3p4nwPXqF1FbiAimv9S":{"to":"aa6055acd1b6e26f5","summary":"Fix review findings in VR-2 ACP half","message":"More follow-up work in /home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2 (branch v1/vr2-verify-for-clients, HEAD f25030a3; start with `git status` and `git log --oneline -5`; do not commit or push; same working rules as before). Another agent added the ACP half of VR-2 in commit fc63f747: an ACP extension method `_nexus/verify` in `cli/src/acp_stdio.ts` (+ `cli/src/acp/{types,validate,mapping}.ts`, schema `docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v2.schema.json` generated by `cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs`, l