{"parentUuid":"735db12a-ff18-43b5-9199-3c7b9cb1d458","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLcb8tRsDEVX3Fv5UWtG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MZrzGt2KY6dn8zqFRuWvow","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #758 PA-3 goals","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #758 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 758`, `gh pr diff 758`), title \"fix(goal): pause stale boot goals with visible reason (PA-3 …)\", base `release/v1.3.0`, branch `v1/pa3-goal-semantics`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 758 --json headRefOid` and review exactly that; say if it moves. Files: `cli/src/core/operation.ts`, `operation_runner.ts`, `operation_schema.ts`, `cli/src/goal.ts`, `goal_command.ts`, `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`, `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`.\n\nThe plan unit (read `git show origin/release/v1.3.0:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`, search \"PA-3\", and the existing `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` on the base): acceptance is \"a stale goal resumes paused; a model's 'done' does not complete it\". Earlier work landed in PR #706; this PR should finish \"paused-on-restart and the lifecycle tests\".\n\nAnswer with file:line evidence, running things where practical:\n1. After a restart (process boot with a persisted goal that was active), is the goal reliably PAUSED with a visible reason, and never silently resumed or left \"running\" with nothing driving it? Cover: crash mid-turn, clean exit, a goal already paused/completed/cancelled (must not change), a goal from an older schema version, a corrupt or truncated state file (fail closed? what does the user see?), two processes booting at once on the same state (races on the state file; is the write atomic?).\n2. Can model output or tool results complete, resume or un-pause a goal? \"Done\"/\"complete\" text from the model, a tool call the model can issue, a crafted goal text, or content in the workspace must not change the lifecycle state; only the operator (and the verified-completion path that already existed) may. Trace who calls each state transition.\n3. Does anything here loosen an approval gate, a budget (the P10 invocation/inference budgets in `cli/src/core`), or the managed policy (`cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts`)? Does resuming a paused goal re-check them?\n4. Schema: `operation_schema.ts` changes — backward compatible with state written by the release branch before this PR? Version bumped/recorded where the repo records it? Any migration?\n5. Tests: do the new lifecycle tests fail if the pause-on-boot logic is removed, and if a model \"done\" is allowed to complete the goal? Mutate (then `git checkout`) and run `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`. Run every `cli/test/goal*.test.ts` and `cli/test/operation*.test.ts` file at head one at a time; for any failure check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n6. Does the doc claim only what the tests show?\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev758 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev758/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev758/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev758`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. Hard timeout on every experiment; no background loops. Aim for about 30 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; findings ranked with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs non-blocking; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2633,"cache_read_input_tokens":449620,"output_tokens":2123,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2633,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2123,"cache_read_input_tokens":449620,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2633},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":14832,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MZrzGt2KY6dn8zqFRuWvow":{"description":"Review PR #758 PA-3 goals","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #758 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 758`, `gh pr diff 758`), title \"fix(goal): pause stale boot goals with visible reason (PA-3 …)\", base `release/v1.3.0`, branch `v1/pa3-goal-semantics`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 758 --json headRefOid` and review exactly that; say if it moves. Files: `cli/src/core/operation.ts`, `operation_runner.ts`, `operation_schema.ts`, `cli/src/goal.ts`, `goal_command.ts`, `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`, `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`.\n\nThe plan unit (read `git show origin/release/v1.3.0:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`, search \"PA-3\", and the existing `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` on the base): acceptance is \"a st