{"parentUuid":"34a9771b-56dd-45c7-9efe-d229cce1b5d6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context."],"hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FaGVdc5riHeu44yLwyLTQy","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","hookKinds":["SettingsHookText"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ea5f184d-058f-42e2-bffa-a5d9b126827f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:02:51.387Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPreToolUse:Bash hook additional context: graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"f2f892b1-3a11-4a25-b2a2-762ab8998377","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"105b53b8-833a-4902-bafe-8b0101ae9bdb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FaGVdc5riHeu44yLwyLTQy","type":"tool_result","content":"7:> and the doctor findings are not in yet: a key marked \"not yet\" below is accepted and merged, and changes nothing.\n8:> Where a behaviour still needs a later change, the text says \"planned\".\n18:| `approval.strict`, `disable_auto`, `disable_yes`, `disable_full_access` | yes | An explicit `--yes`, `--mode auto` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` is refused at launch (exit 2). During a session a switch to `auto` (`/mode auto`, an \"always\" answer) is ignor\n27:| `egress.secret_destinations` | not yet | Nothing reads it. |\n30:| `mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace` | not yet | Planned (GV-5). |\n31:| `plugins.allow`, `plugins.disable_workspace` | not yet | Planned (GV-5). |\n37:  yet, and `sandbox.*` does not reach `nexus verify --sandbox` yet (planned).\n39:  session, also under `approval.disable_auto` (planned). The line-mode REPL asks every time.\n349:  its own yet: it shows the error in its configuration finding. A `nexus policy check` command is planned.\n360:- `nexus doctor --fix` is not to modify a policy file (planned).\n399:  Nexus does not yet show the relaxations when it records an approval, and does not yet ask in the middle of a\n400:  session (planned); read the file before you trust the workspace.\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to Nexus Code are documented in this file.\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n\nDetailed per-release documentation is maintained in [`docs/releases/`](docs/releases/).\n\n## [v1.2.2] - 2026-11-21\n\n### Changed\n- VC-8: the implementer and tester roles are refused the tools that reach outside the task. Both lose the browser tools and `manage_knowledge`; the tester also loses `fetch_web`, `search_web` and `spawn_subagent`. The agent neither offers a refused tool nor runs it when the model calls it anyway; the denial names the role and sa\n- Redaction variants (MT-3, part 2): `formatSafeSidecarText` calls the shared `safeTerminal` instead of restating it, with output byte-identical; the remaining variants are kept and each has a reason in `docs/v1.2.1/REDACTION_VARIANTS.md`. New `cli/test/mt3_redaction_characterization.test.ts` pins the exact output of 23 redactio\n\n### Added\n- VC-9 (the two remaining cases): in `nexus run`, a requirement the model marks blocked now ends the run `BLOCKED / NEEDS_INPUT` (`kind: blocked_requirement`) with the blocker as the question, answered in free text with `--answer <id>=reply:<text>`; before it ended `COMPLETED / REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE` with the reason only in a \n- CS-10 (Docker and phase 2): on Linux, `--sandbox docker` now runs the native worker inside the hardened container as well (before, Docker confined commands only and the worker kept the operator's access). The worker is mounted read-only with the loader and libraries it was linked against in a private directory, so it starts in\n- Significant independent reviews now require eight non-empty engineering-assessment fields when a diff touches core code, five or more files, or at least 300 added/removed lines. The parser derives significance from the diff, fails closed on malformed or incomplete assessments, and never lets the assessment override verifier, s\n- CS-9: operator command rules in `~/.config/nexus/command_rules.json` (operator home only; a project file is never read). Prefix rules decide a shell command as `allow` (no prompt in review mode), `prompt` (asks even in auto mode, unless `--yes`) or `forbidden` (refused in every mode); the strictest rule wins. `allow` needs eve\n- VC-2: an authorised regression obligation is discharged only when the verifier output reports a recognised result for that exact test. A green suite that does not show the test, a skipped result, and older pass records without test-name binding remain unresolved and block completion.\n- CS-11: a command that fails with only volatile text changing (a retry counter, request or job number, ephemeral port, temp directory name, counter after a transfer verb, compound duration; an HTTP status, a build step index and outcome counts stay distinct) is now the same failure to the non-progress tracker and to CS-3: it is\n- VC-9: a delegated subagent's headless decision (tool approval, verification-file edit, verifier approval) is no longer lost. The subagent stops at it and returns the question (same id and shape, plus `subagent: { depth, objective }`) to its parent, whose headless run ends BLOCKED / NEEDS_INPUT; `--answer` resumes it (the re-sp\n\n### Fixed\n- A failing type-check whose output is coloured is `FAILED`, not `ENVIRONMENT`. With `FORCE_COLOR=1` in the operator's environment `tsc` wraps the file, line and column in escape sequences; the diagnostics parser then located no file and the check was classified \"could not run\", which does not block completion (VC-6, CG-4). Esca\n- A native worker that exits right after launch (for example a Docker worker whose container fails to start) no longer raises an uncaught `EPIPE` that ended the CLI: the worker's stdin stream has an error listener and the waiting request is answered as a disconnect.\n- Saving progress no longer fails on a worktree binding left over from an earlier turn (\"Task state worktree path has no selected workspace identity\"); it showed only when the workspace directory name tripped the secret classifier's high-entropy check.\n- VC-6: Cargo projects are part of the pre-change type-check baseline (the per-workspace target directory is reused, so dependencies are not built twice); a regression case covers a pre-existing Rust diagnostic against a new one in an untouched caller.\n- MCP and plugin tools now run. They were offered to the model but never registered in the capability registry, so the execution spine answered every call with `FAIL-001: Tool ... is not registered`; the server never received `tools/call`. They are now registered after connection as `extension` capabilities with conservative def\n- The real language-server job's Rust setup: rust-analyzer is now added to the default toolchain (the product launches servers outside the repository, where the repository's pinned toolchain does not apply), and the test's availability probe runs in the fixture directory, as the product does.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fa0aac6c-d418-41e0-8c76-f11efb594fa6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:02:52.623Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"7:> and the doctor findings are not in yet: a key marked \"not yet\" below is accepted and merged, and changes nothing.\n8:> Where a behaviour still needs a later change, the text says \"planned\".\n18:| `approval.strict`, `disable_auto`, `disable_yes`, `disable_full_access` | yes | An explicit `--yes`, `--mode auto` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` is refused at launch (exit 2). During a session a switch to `auto` (`/mode auto`, an \"always\" answer) is ignor\n27:| `egress.secret_destinations` | not yet | Nothing reads it. |\n30:| `mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace` | not yet | Planned (GV-5). |\n31:| `plugins.allow`, `plugins.disable_workspace` | not yet | Planned (GV-5). |\n37:  yet, and `sandbox.*` does not reach `nexus verify --sandbox` yet (planned).\n39:  session, also under `approval.disable_auto` (planned). The line-mode REPL asks every time.\n349:  its own yet: it shows the error in its configuration finding. A `nexus policy check` command is planned.\n360:- `nexus doctor --fix` is not to modify a policy file (planned).\n399:  Nexus does not yet show the relaxations when it records an approval, and does not yet ask in the middle of a\n400:  session (planned); read the file before you trust the workspace.\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to Nexus Code are documented in this file.\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n\nDetailed per-release documentation is maintained in [`docs/releases/`](docs/releases/).\n\n## [v1.2.2] - 2026-11-21\n\n### Changed\n- VC-8: the implementer and tester roles are refused the tools that reach outside the task. Both lose the browser tools and `manage_knowledge`; the tester also loses `fetch_web`, `search_web` and `spawn_subagent`. The agent neither offers a refused tool nor runs it when the model calls it anyway; the denial names the role and sa\n- Redaction variants (MT-3, part 2): `formatSafeSidecarText` calls the shared `safeTerminal` instead of restating it, with output byte-identical; the remaining variants are kept and each has a reason in `docs/v1.2.1/REDACTION_VARIANTS.md`. New `cli/test/mt3_redaction_characterization.test.ts` pins the exact output of 23 redactio\n\n### Added\n- VC-9 (the two remaining cases): in `nexus run`, a requirement the model marks blocked now ends the run `BLOCKED / NEEDS_INPUT` (`kind: blocked_requirement`) with the blocker as the question, answered in free text with `--answer <id>=reply:<text>`; before it ended `COMPLETED / REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE` with the reason only in a \n- CS-10 (Docker and phase 2): on Linux, `--sandbox docker` now runs the native worker inside the hardened container as well (before, Docker confined commands only and the worker kept the operator's access). The worker is mounted read-only with the loader and libraries it was linked against in a private directory, so it starts in\n- Significant independent reviews now require eight non-empty engineering-assessment fields when a diff touches core code, five or more files, or at least 300 added/removed lines. The parser derives significance from the diff, fails closed on malformed or incomplete assessments, and never lets the assessment override verifier, s\n- CS-9: operator command rules in `~/.config/nexus/command_rules.json` (operator home only; a project file is never read). Prefix rules decide a shell command as `allow` (no prompt in review mode), `prompt` (asks even in auto mode, unless `--yes`) or `forbidden` (refused in every mode); the strictest rule wins. `allow` needs eve\n- VC-2: an authorised regression obligation is discharged only when the verifier output reports a recognised result for that exact test. A green suite that does not show the test, a skipped result, and older pass records without test-name binding remain unresolved and block completion.\n- CS-11: a command that fails with only volatile text changing (a retry counter, request or job number, ephemeral port, temp directory name, counter after a transfer verb, compound duration; an HTTP status, a build step index and outcome counts stay distinct) is now the same failure to the non-progress tracker and to CS-3: it is\n- VC-9: a delegated subagent's headless decision (tool approval, verification-file edit, verifier approval) is no longer lost. The subagent stops at it and returns the question (same id and shape, plus `subagent: { depth, objective }`) to its parent, whose headless run ends BLOCKED / NEEDS_INPUT; `--answer` resumes it (the re-sp\n\n### Fixed\n- A failing type-check whose output is coloured is `FAILED`, not `ENVIRONMENT`. With `FORCE_COLOR=1` in the operator's environment `tsc` wraps the file, line and column in escape sequences; the diagnostics parser then located no file and the check was classified \"could not run\", which does not block completion (VC-6, CG-4). Esca\n- A native worker that exits right after launch (for example a Docker worker whose container fails to start) no longer raises an uncaught `EPIPE` that ended the CLI: the worker's stdin stream has an error listener and the waiting request is answered as a disconnect.\n- Saving progress no longer fails on a worktree binding left over from an earlier turn (\"Task state