{"parentUuid":"93e6aa70-3fb8-49fa-aed8-d43c0ce73365","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLcfmFJqvcHtApExhELH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is where things stand after the quota pause.\n\n**What changed while I was out**\n- **VR-2 was taken over by owner direction** (logged 19:55Z), and #756 was merged by another session at 21:24Z. I've stopped all VR-2 work and hold no unit claim. I'm reading that takeover as your answer that units stay with Codex, so I'm back to merge queue, review and CI only.\n- **#756 merged with six review follow-ups still open.** The second independent review found no blocker but did find real weaknesses in the ACP half; I've posted them on the PR for Codex. The weightiest:\n  - a new ACP session re-pins the verification base, so a client can commit weakened tests and then open a new session;\n  - the client chooses which directory is verified, and the result doesn't name it;\n  - `_nexus/receipt/get` without an id now returns verification receipts, which changes behaviour for existing clients.\n- **The follow-ups from the first review are in what merged:** SIGTERM cleanup for the verifier, read-only honoured from the environment, and fuller documented limits.\n\n**Queue now**\n- **#757 (readiness inventory and changelog):** I posted a request for changes. It lists GV-1 and GV-5 as landed, but the release branch's own `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md` marks the MCP and plugin allowlists \"not yet\" and the `nexus policy` commands and doctor findings as not in. It also omits SB-1, MT-1 and MT-2, and lists VR-2 as landed without the open follow-ups.\n- **#758 (PA-3, stale goals pause on restart):** an independent review is running.\n- **Release branch:** green at `56e644cf`.\n\n**One thing for you:** #741, #749, #754 and #756 were merged by other sessions outside the queue, two of them over standing review findings. If that is how you want it, tell me and I'll stop treating the queue as mine; otherwise the other sessions need to stop merging."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":461500,"output_tokens":649,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1122,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":461500,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1122},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLcfm2fYQ6B3vVrHSfaP","requestRef":"e5c5fd2c-0d1e-4ffe-ad53-3fa6db876563","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f170044-c81d-45b3-ba2b-0960095ea695","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:03:29.223Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
