{"parentUuid":"b63c861c-b60e-4059-8568-8f84f3430bfe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLeVZjiXAuiMbwBdK2H2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018E5VP5zBeYJcoQgHV8TTpV","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #760 inference budget","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #760 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 760`, `gh pr diff 760`), title \"feat(budget): bound objective inference submissions\", base `release/v1.3.0`, branch `v1/p10-02-inference-submission-budget`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 760 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check again at the end whether it moved. Files include `cli/src/config.ts`, `cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts`, `cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts`, `cli/src/core/run_turn.ts`, `cli/src/core/turn.ts`, `cli/src/doctor.ts`, `cli/src/types.ts`, `cli/test/p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts`, docs and protocol ledgers/schemas (`docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, `VERSIONS.json`, `run-result-v1.schema…`).\n\nContext: work package WP-P10-02 in `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (\"aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths\"). An earlier PR bounded tool invocations (search the repo for `p10` tests, e.g. `cli/test/p10_*.test.ts`, and the merged tool-invocation budget). This PR bounds the number of inference (model) submissions per objective.\n\nAnswer with file:line evidence, running things where practical:\n1. Is the bound aggregate and unbypassable? Count every path that submits to the model: the normal turn loop, retries after provider errors (`provider_recovery.ts`), fallback/alternate providers, compaction/summarisation calls, title or classifier side calls if any, delegated subagents (`spawn_subagent` and the operation runner), resumed sessions (does the counter persist across `--resume` / a restarted process, or reset to zero?), and steering/continuations. Which are counted, which are not, and is each omission stated in the docs? Can a model or workspace content reset or raise the budget (config from the project directory, env files in the workspace, tool calls)? Who may configure it (operator home vs project) and what are the defaults, minimum and maximum? Is an invalid value fail-closed?\n2. What happens at the limit: the turn must end in a defined, visible state (which execution/reason?), with no further submission, and must not be reported as COMPLETED/VERIFIED. Does anything retry after the limit? Off-by-one at the boundary (limit N allows exactly N submissions)?\n3. Does it interact safely with the existing tool-invocation budget, the managed policy (`cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts`: can policy only tighten?), and approval gates? Anything loosened?\n4. Schema/protocol: `run-result` schema and version ledgers — additive and versioned per the repo's rules (frozen older versions untouched; see how `docs/protocol/*VERSIONS.json` and their tests work)? `nexus doctor` output change consistent?\n5. Tests: would `cli/test/p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts` fail if (a) the check were removed, (b) retries were not counted, (c) the counter reset on resume? Mutate one at a time (then `git checkout`) and run it. Run at head, one file at a time: that file, the other `cli/test/p10_*.test.ts` files, `cli/test/run_contract*.test.ts` or whatever tests the run-result schema, `cli/test/protocol_parity.test.ts`, `cli/test/context_convergence.test.ts`, `cli/test/doctor*.test.ts` (those that exist). For any failure, check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n6. Do the docs claim only what the code and tests show?\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev760 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev760/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev760/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev760`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, each with a timeout of at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`; `eval_*` tests fail locally, ignore them). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 35 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 550 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; findings ranked with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs non-blocking; the list of submission paths with counted / not counted; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":622,"cache_read_input_tokens":478831,"output_tokens":2049,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":622,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2049,"cache_read_input_tokens":478831,"cache_creation_input_tokens":622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":622},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17611,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu