{"parentUuid":"25379d0c-c609-40a0-88b5-6866049d6321","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLey33XzUeoH2vFojSy9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #760 review is in and posted on the PR as request changes, with one blocker.\n\n- **Blocker:** a stale test fixture. The PR changed the sidecar schema but didn't regenerate the schema samples, so `protocol_parity` fails at its head and passes on the release branch. Regenerating the fixture fixes it. CI is red on four test legs; the run was still in progress, so I haven't read those logs and can't say whether this is the only cause.\n- **The budget logic held up:**\n  - At the limit the turn ends in a defined, non-completed state.\n  - Nothing retries after the limit.\n  - A limit of N allows exactly N submissions.\n  - The counter survives a resume and can only be lowered.\n  - Removing the check, not counting retries, or resetting on resume each fails the new tests.\n- **Docs should say what the bound doesn't cover:** subagents and operation units are documented as uncounted, but three side calls that also hit the model are not mentioned (findings extraction and two compaction calls). A project `.env` can also raise the ceiling from 1,000 to 10,000, which the docs don't say.\n\nQueue: #758 and #760 are both waiting on their author. The release branch is at `24992b1f` after the inventory correction; its CI is running and I'll read it before the next merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":486609,"output_tokens":424,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2009,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":424,"cache_read_input_tokens":486609,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2009},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLey2r8kDJgB7iR3Dbph","requestRef":"3661333c-6231-49b3-bb88-785d33a35cbe","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"89841bab-3f85-4e31-b175-aab4bec84b3f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:33:34.990Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
