mit `7320b78a` (rolled-up sub-operation token usage in `cli/src/goal.ts`, `goal_command.ts`): any way it misreports, double counts, or exposes data it should not? Light check.\n6. Run at head, one file at a time: every `cli/test/goal*.test.ts` and `cli/test/operation*.test.ts`; for any failure check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev758b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev758b/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev758b/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev758b`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Probe scripts live in a separate scratch directory. Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 30 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; each blocker fixed / partly / not with file:line and what you ran; status of the non-blocking items; new findings ranked, blocking vs not; mutation result; test counts; what you did not check."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChLf7rmuMEfTvuPj39cgc","requestRef":"2c2ae1a7-7bb2-42d7-8b41-122430b42fa0","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc6f18f8-c66a-4b1c-b209-71463ef49b5a","timestam