{"parentUuid":"0e83029c-7ae1-4c11-acef-d67fa442df51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLfqZJ6hgXtXGfEuXPW1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CNWrszuSK1mmj76NF7WK8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 760 --body \"**Re-review at \\`f4abea7a97b4cb21dc44a719ff46b37ca1a928af\\` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head has since moved to \\`03452d17\\`, which changes one line of the new test file (the leak-guard registration) and nothing else, so item 1 still applies.**\n\n1. **Still failing: the schema samples fixture.** \\`protocol_parity\\` fails 1 of 5 (\\\"checked-in schema samples equal a fresh generation\\\"). \\`node cli/scripts/gen_protocol_samples.mjs --check\\` reports the fixture out of date; running it without \\`--check\\` changes two lines of \\`cli/test/fixtures/protocol_v1_schema_samples.jsonl\\` (the \\`history\\` full samples gain \\`inferenceSubmissions\\`, \\`inferenceSubmissionHistoryComplete\\` and \\`maxInferenceSubmissions\\`). Commit that. The Rust test \\`schema_samples_parse_as_their_own_event_variants\\` reads the same fixture; the new fields are nested, so no Rust change is expected, but cargo was not run here.\n2. **Leak guard** (\\\"the leak ratchet holds\\\" failed with \\`missing: ['p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts']\\` at \\`f4abea7a\\`): \\`03452d17\\` appears to address this; CI on that head will show it.\n\nCI at \\`75a838be\\` failed on four tests: the two ACP schema checks (fixed by \\`f4abea7a\\`: \\`acp_schema\\` 7/7), the samples fixture (item 1) and the leak ratchet (item 2).\n\nDocs: retries, persistence and the primary-turn scope are now stated, and the plan note says delegated paths remain outside the bound. Still not stated: findings extraction and the two compaction calls are uncounted, and a project \\`.env\\` can set \\`NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS\\`.\n\nThe budget itself is unchanged by the delta: \\`p10_i