{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChLju4gVCKpKjw285h3Nm","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["msg_011ChLjoppR7gvbtBudRfuCp"]}]}
{"parentUuid":"76657cc8-cf34-4126-b8a2-c13aafbe9826","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLju4gVCKpKjw285h3Nm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#761 is merged and the release branch is green at `14410b32`. One PR is open: #758 (PA-3), still waiting on its author.\n\n**#761 (flight recorder), merged after review**\n- **What it does:** when the recorder can't redact or append a record, it reports the skip and stops chaining, so a log with a gap followed by later records reads as broken rather than intact. The new tests fail when that logic is removed.\n- **Follow-ups posted on the PR, none blocking:**\n  - **A restart can hide a skip.** If the skipped record was the last event before the process stopped, a new process resumes the chain from the last good record and the log reads as intact.\n  - **The operator isn't told.** Nothing warns when recording degrades; the only trace is the unchained log read later.\n  - **An input can trigger it.** A cyclic or BigInt argument makes redaction fail and degrades recording for the rest of the session. Arguments parsed from JSON can't take either form, and the reviewer did not trace whether a model can reach that path.\n  - **`audit verify` is lenient.** It treats a log that was already broken at export as a note, not a failure.\n\n**Merged by me since the pause, each after review:** #759 (inventory corrections), #760 (inference budget) and #761.\n\n**Still not done for v1.3.0**\n- Unbuilt: PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, BG-1, BG-2, HK-1 to HK-3, PA-2.\n- Unfinished: GV-1 slices 3–4, the GV-5 allowlists, the six VR-2 follow-ups, and PA-3 (#758).\n- Yours: which units roll to v1.4, and the go-ahead for the merge to `main` and the tag."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":520487,"output_tokens":571,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1184,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":520487,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1184},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLju4U5VWupxdXoM1T9s","requestRef":"feeb913d-579d-4740-8bc2-9343d4da90da","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a63dbfed-c7b6-4356-9206-f48b2d9f4113","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:38:16.587Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
