{"parentUuid":"8d9c6eb6-dcc4-438e-91bf-79212a7e20f5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FXKKxwW9GwEJMFn7mtx8sY","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":335},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5becdeeb-f2c8-40d0-b815-8a4e1281046f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:46:19.024Z","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"8d9c6eb6-dcc4-438e-91bf-79212a7e20f5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9e18ce2f-d25b-4566-85bc-e814aa7dff3b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXKKxwW9GwEJMFn7mtx8sY","type":"tool_result","content":"main\tv1/p10-02-active-deadline\t56\t2\tfix(agent): enforce active turn deadline during async calls\tcli/src/core/run_turn.ts,cli/test/turn_deadline_abort.test.ts\n## Summary\n\nEnforce the existing `maxTurnMinutes` deadline while asynchronous work is in flight. When the deadline expires, the active turn is aborted and reported as `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; ordinary operator cancellation keeps its existing `OPERATOR_INTERRUPT` result. The deadline timer is cleared on normal completion and error paths.\n\nThis is one bounded P10-02 slice. Durable cumulative elapsed accounting across multiple turns/resumes, and independent per-tool deadlines, remain open work.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- `test/turn_deadline_abort.test.ts` — passed under Node 22.22.2 and Node 24.21.0 with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\nThe test holds a local streaming inference request open, then verifies the configured one-minute-fraction deadline aborts it promptly and yields a non-success budget result. During development, a single Node 22 run of the original delayed-response fixture exceeded its timing assertion; I changed the fixture to a slow stream that exits after the client aborts, and the final fixture passed on both","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8f4e4854-30b4-4aab-9cbd-036e179a26fa","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:46:20.098Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"main\tv1/p10-02-active-deadline\t56\t2\tfix(agent): enforce active turn deadline during async calls\tcli/src/core/run_turn.ts,cli/test/turn_deadline_abort.test.ts\n## Summary\n\nEnforce the existing `maxTurnMinutes` deadline while asynchronous work is in flight. When the deadline expires, the active turn is aborted and reported as `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; ordinary operator cancellation keeps its existing `OPERATOR_INTERRUPT` result. The deadline timer is cleared on normal completion and error paths.\n\nThis is one bounded P10-02 slice. Durable cumulative elapsed accounting across multiple turns/resumes, and independent per-tool deadlines, remain open work.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- `test/turn_deadline_abort.test.ts` — passed under Node 22.22.2 and Node 24.21.0 with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\nThe test holds a local streaming inference request open, then verifies the configured one-minute-fraction deadline aborts it promptly and yields a non-success budget result. During development, a single Node 22 run of the original delayed-response fixture exceeded its timing assertion; I changed the fixture to a slow stream that exits after the client aborts, and the final fixture passed on both","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d9c6eb6-dcc4-438e-91bf-79212a7e20f5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
