{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"a7968a7ef915681c7f9777b2e227ca500dd252042dca227bdc70c5d02aad071f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Teme1nVXxUiB3XJM5tZp6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev758c.md","content":"**Third review at `9b637c48addb2fc788d6b58afa9919d86dd62a32` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, pending green required checks on this head**\n\n**The blocker is fixed.** `operation_entry_integrity.test.ts` passes 3 of 3. `pauseForStaleDriver` now returns early for a RUNNING operation that has never run (every unit `WAITING_ON_DEPENDENCY`, `runs === 0`, no `agentTaskId`). Run against seeded state through the real `driveOperation`: a fresh plan with no identity is not paused; an operation with a started unit and no identity, or with a dead pid, comes back PAUSED.\n\n**The restart protection still holds for goals.** `goalStatus` probed over six statuses and seven identity shapes: RUNNING and WAITING with no identity, a dead pid or an old boot id come back PAUSED; a live owner is left alone; PAUSED, COMPLETE and CANCELLED are untouched. Removing the goal-level check fails `goal_lifecycle` 2 of 7.\n\n**Follow-ups, none blocking**\n\n1. **The `driveOperation` stale path has no test.** Removing the `pauseForStaleDriver` call leaves `goal_lifecycle`, `operation_entry_integrity`, `operation_runner_restart`, `operation_lock`, `operation_concurrency` and `operation_runner_refactor` all green: the two new goal tests use fresh plans, which the new early return skips. Add a test with a started unit (`runs = 1`, dead pid) driven with `entry: \"existing\"`, asserting PAUSED and the \"Paused on resume\" text, and one for the `resumeAfterDecision` handoff.\n2. **The two layers disagree.** `goalStatus` reports PAUSED for a BLOCKED goal with a dead owner and for a never-started plan with no identity; `driveOperation` leaves both alone. The doc's sentence that a BLOCKED operation \"remains at that decision boundary\" is true of `driveOperation` only. Align the checks or word the doc to match.\n3. **Limits the doc still does not state:** a reused pid reads as alive; a state from another host, or with a pid and no host, stays RUNNING.\n4. Unchanged from before: the host-boot test returns early without `/proc`; `pauseReason ?? stale` lets an older operator reason hide the restart reason; the `(state as any)` casts; the reason text is duplicated across `goal.ts` and `operation_runner.ts`.\n\n`policy_runtime.ts` is not in the PR; no path from model text, a tool call or workspace content to a lifecycle change was found by reading. `resumeAfterDecision` stamps the current pid before the stale check and is passed only by `operation decide`.\n\n**Tests at this head, run one file at a time, 0 failures:** `goal_lifecycle` 7, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, thirteen `operation*` files (179 tests), `leak_guard` 6.\n\n**Not checked:** `tsc` (CI runs it), a real process crash (probes used seeded state), the loop and batch resume callers beyond reading, Node 22.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CGxSHAQx7yQ1Lp43AUCkZm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 758 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev758c.md | tail -1; bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 16); do c=$(gh pr checks 758 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 758 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; gh pr checks 758 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 758 --json headRefOid,state --jq \"[.state,.headRefOid]|@tsv\"; git fetch -q origin; echo \"tip $(git rev-parse --short origin/release/v1.3.0)\"; m=$(gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pulls/758 --jq .merge_commit_sha); git fetch -q origin $m 2>/dev/null; echo \"merge parents: $(git log -1 --format=%P $m | tr \" \" \"\\n\" | cut -c1-8 | tr \"\\n\" \" \")\"; gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \".[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv\"'","description":"Post the third review on PR 758, wait for its checks, and re-read the release state","timeout":560000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
