{"parentUuid":"f3d16273-76e7-4fc2-8a38-6b329e40d740","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fe8cdc99-57c4-4dc1-a999-66e8e4b40dda","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvVysv7K8CXrxWNGwxUt6r","type":"tool_result","content":"5e5bb11f fix(audit): fail closed on flight recording gaps\n+  /** A flight log records that one or more events could not be recorded, even if no chained record precedes the gap. */\n+  | \"log_recording_gap_at_export\"\n+      const hasRecordingGap = recorded.kind === \"flight\" && read.records.some((record) =>\n+        isObject(record) && record.type === \"recording_gap\" && isObject(record.payload) && record.payload.recordingSkipped === true,\n+      );\n+      if (hasRecordingGap) {\n+        findings.add(\"log_recording_gap_at_export\", `${recorded.path} records that one or more events were skipped; its source evidence is incomplete.`, recorded.path);\n+      }\n+If flight recording fails and the recorder cannot persist its gap marker either, a later process cannot infer from the log alone that an event was skipped. The operator warning reports the recording failure at the time, but no durable log evidence exists for that failure. Keep the warning and external process logs with the expo\n+The finding set is additive within schema version 1. Consumers that validate `finding.kind` against an older, closed enum must update their schema before accepting `log_recording_gap_at_export`. Verification can also change a prior bundle's result from `intact_unsigned` to `tampered` when the bundle already recorded a broken so\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"schema_version\": 1,\n+    \"schemaSha256\": \"18a4b9660a68eb5e1e486353c03778c4eb1af2fd045d0985fad7188feddebf1c\",\n+    \"note\": \"Additive P10-03 follow-up: audit verification reports durable flight recording-gap markers as findings, including a marker before any chained record; schema_version remains 1.\"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"901793d7-41d2-4291-9a0c-209c4f921e12","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:56:30.115Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"5e5bb11f fix(audit): fail closed on flight recording gaps\n+  /** A flight log records that one or more events could not be recorded, even if no chained record precedes the gap. */\n+  | \"log_recording_gap_at_export\"\n+      const hasRecordingGap = recorded.kind === \"flight\" && read.records.some((record) =>\n+        isObject(record) && record.type === \"recording_gap\" && isObject(record.payload) && record.payload.recordingSkipped === true,\n+      );\n+      if (hasRecordingGap) {\n+        findings.add(\"log_recording_gap_at_export\", `${recorded.path} records that one or more events were skipped; its source evidence is incomplete.`, recorded.path);\n+      }\n+If flight recording fails and the recorder cannot persist its gap marker either, a later process cannot infer from the log alone that an event was skipped. The operator warning reports the recording failure at the time, but no durable log evidence exists for that failure. Keep the warning and external process logs with the expo\n+The finding set is additive within schema version 1. Consumers that validate `finding.kind` against an older, closed enum must update their schema before accepting `log_recording_gap_at_export`. Verification can also change a prior bundle's result from `intact_unsigned` to `tampered` when the bundle already recorded a broken so\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"schema_version\": 1,\n+    \"schemaSha256\": \"18a4b9660a68eb5e1e486353c03778c4eb1af2fd045d0985fad7188feddebf1c\",\n+    \"note\": \"Additive P10-03 follow-up: audit verification reports durable flight recording-gap markers as findings, including a marker before any chained record; schema_version remains 1.\"","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f3d16273-76e7-4fc2-8a38-6b329e40d740","permissionDecision":{