{"parentUuid":"25be89c7-d725-4423-9358-94c686b0731e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM2EQ8v7Cxj6PNqG7FFP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BUKBhKfr4zpV1frBx7KS5o","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev766.md","content":"**Independent review at `23a563ff31383136d7ad3b93ec59410f39bac631` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, pending green required checks**\n\n**Dependency.** `@babel/parser` 7.29.15, pinned, in `devDependencies`. The lockfile gains four packages, all `\"dev\": true`, MIT, none with an install script. `scripts/package-linux.sh` installs with `npm ci --omit=dev` and builds notices with `--production`, so none of them reaches the release tarball or the notices. `check_deprecated_lock.mjs` passes; no `engines.node` field changed.\n\n**Where it runs.** `make lint` (`Makefile:26`), so `test-gates` on Node 22 and 24; not in the packaging job, not in `release.yml`. About 3.7 s. `release_workflow_parity` 6/6.\n\n**What it checks.** Cyclomatic complexity and maximum control nesting for five listed functions (`runTurnImpl` among them), each compared with its own source at a pinned baseline revision; any increase exits 1. Malformed baseline, an unknown or ambiguous function, or a baseline revision that is not a 40-hex ancestor of `HEAD` exits 2. Renaming a listed function gives exit 2 (run). The five functions measure equal to baseline at this head (CC 324, 288, 70, 17, 17), matching the plan text.\n\n**Follow-ups, none blocking**\n\n1. **Inline callbacks are not measured** (`measureNode` returns at any nested function). Moving a nested `if` into an inline arrow function leaves the enclosing function's numbers unchanged and the gate at exit 0 (run). Count nested functions into the enclosing one, or say so where the metric is described.\n2. **`?.`, `||=`, `&&=` and `??=` are not counted** (run: adding them changes nothing).\n3. **Test gaps** (run): making `main()` always return 0 fails no test; making the check compare current source with current source fails no test, because baseline and current are identical today. A temporary-repository fixture with a regressed function would cover both.\n4. **Nothing pins the wiring**: deleting the gate from the `Makefile` leaves `release_workflow_parity` at 6/6. Add an assertion that `make lint` runs the script.\n5. The plan's acceptance says \"crossing a threshold\"; the implementation is \"any increase over baseline\". Align the wording.\n6. The new test file has no entry in `test_durations.json`; the sharder falls back to file size.\n\nKnown limits, as the plan says: extracting a helper that is not on the list passes, line growth is reported and not enforced, and the baseline or the list can be edited in the same PR (visible in review).\n\n**Run at this head:** `critical_complexity` 3/3, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `leak_guard` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `check_deprecated_lock` and `check_invariants` pass. The gate's mutation: making the comparison never flag fails 1 test.\n\n**Not run:** clippy and the rustfmt check (the rest of `make lint`; CI runs them), a fresh `npm ci` (no network: the check was run with the same package versions copied from another worktree).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":597329,"output_tokens":2078,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2078,"cache_read_input_tokens":597329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_t