{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"72f2a8ae09d71fa056aab1468395bc2629b9667d2f4beeefaf52a7d0df48da00","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lr1z88bmDLsikkGwvfbvcM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev770.md","content":"**Independent review at `20b50f9bbb63bf29c668d76504160db8971dad68` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS; the follow-ups are applied in `c152d160` (the commit before the merge of the release branch).**\n\n**Found, and now fixed**\n\n1. **The worker's pid was signalled after the worker had exited.** The sweep in `finish` always runs after the worker is reaped, and the timed stages can fire between `exit` and `disconnect`; both sent SIGSTOP and SIGCONT to a pid that could have been reused, and used it as a root, so a reused process's children could have been stopped and killed. Rare (pids are reused after a wrap), not impossible in a container with a small `pid_max`. Now: once `child.exitCode` or `child.signalCode` is set, the worker's pid is neither signalled nor searched; only remembered survivors are roots.\n2. **Processes added by the last listing were neither stopped nor signalled** when the pass limit was hit. They are now signalled with the rest.\n3. **The server's exit handler could take up to seven process listings** (35 s if `ps` hangs). It now takes at most two.\n\n**Held up**\n\n- `startedAt` reads the right field for a process named `a) b 1 2 3` (run). A pid whose start time cannot be read is never remembered, so `undefined` is never compared. Roots are the worker and remembered survivors, and only their children are followed: init's other children, the server and the client cannot be pulled in.\n- Nothing is left stopped: the SIGTERM stage continues everything it stopped; the spared-worker kill continues the worker; the full kill kills everything. A failed or timed-out `ps` yields an empty listing, and only the worker is stopped and then continued or killed. A loop with a stopped-process check: 60 runs, 0 orphans, 0 left in state `T`.\n- The graceful path still works: the worker is stopped, SIGTERM is queued, SIGCONT follows, and the handler runs. The scratch-removal assertions pass after cancellation (`verify_service.test.ts:252`, `mcp_verify.test.ts:112`), after the watchdog timeout (`verify_service.test.ts:288`) and on SIGTERM to the server (`mcp_verify.test.ts:311`).\n- The reviewer's own loop at `20b50f9b`: 120 runs with a SIGTERM-ignoring verifier, 0 orphans.\n\n**After the fixes, run by me at `c152d160`'s parent commit:** `verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7, `tsc` clean, and another 150 cancellations with 0 orphans.\n\n**Still open, not blocking**\n\n- `seen` is not pruned during a run (bounded by one verification).\n- Unit tests that could be added deterministically: `startedAt` parsing with `)` and spaces in the name; `descendants` with several roots and with a reparented root.\n- Not checked: Node 22 locally, the Docker sandbox engine, a `ps` that hangs.\n\nThe three fixes were made after the review and have not themselves been reviewed by a second reader; they are small and each follows the reviewer's stated fix.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019pV5XxbxgUFghxC1Ymf32p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 770 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev770.md | tail -1; bash -c 'sleep 30; for i in $(seq 1 17); do st=$(gh pr view 770 --json state --jq .state); c=$(gh pr checks 770 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 770 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); r=$(gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \".[0]|.status+\\\"/\\\"+(.conclusion//\\\"\\\")+\\\"/\\\"+.headSha[0:8]\"); [ \"$st\" != OPEN ] && break; [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && [ \"${r%%/*}\" = completed ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; echo \"state $st pass $c fail $f release $r\"; gh pr checks 770 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 770 --json headRefOid --jq .headRefOid; git fetch -q origin; echo \"tip $(git rev-parse --short origin/release/v1.3.0)\"'","description":"Post the review and the fixes on PR 770, then wait for its checks and the release CI","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
