{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChMGQ9ZiSDVEaNiBoitwr","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["REDACTED"]}]}
{"parentUuid":"79f2c287-5cde-4d34-92ce-7b3f4def74d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMGQ9ZiSDVEaNiBoitwr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #771 re-review is posted on the PR as request changes. **This PR should not be merged on green checks**, and it is close to having them.\n\n- **The blocker is untouched.** Every commit since the first review only changes test expectations; the source is the same. The checks will go green because no test exercises a hostile workspace.\n- **Nine git-configuration vectors run a workspace-configured program during `audit export`**, each confirmed by running. They include a clean filter, a process filter, `core.fsmonitor`, config includes, attributes files, and a `.git` file pointing at another git directory, which also passes the existing checkout-trust check. Hooks, text conversion, pager and editor settings did not execute.\n- **The exposure is wider than this PR.** The candidate-identity routine is shared with the agent, worktree, state and operation code, so the same hole exists wherever a candidate identity is computed. This PR adds a new place to reach it, one an auditor would run on a workspace they don't trust. I've flagged that for whoever owns the routine.\n\nI've put a second do-not-merge note in the claims log. If #771 gets merged outside the queue anyway, as seven PRs have been, I'll open a fix immediately.\n\nThe release branch is unchanged and green at `5abbc4cb`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":686974,"output_tokens":413,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"outp