{"parentUuid":"1f48128c-96ca-4fee-89f2-24bf31a08534","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMKBDY5XExWvTPub97dn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012wWxQK1eGAEQ35eJ1crM3J","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/cgit && git status --short | head -3 && git commit -qam \"test(audit): quote the included filter command so it is not cut at the semicolon\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q origin v1/audit-binding-refuse-repo-programs 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/audit-binding-refuse-repo-programs | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 771 --body \"**Check at \\`3600eefd\\` (\\\"disable repository fsmonitor during identity reads\\\") — still REQUEST CHANGES: one of the vectors is closed, the filters are not.**\n\nMeasured by running the real \\`exportAuditBundle\\` on a seeded subject whose workspace has a committed file with an unchanged size and a bumped modification time (so Git must re-hash it), with a planted command that writes a marker file:\n\n| Planted in the repository's own configuration | At \\`3600eefd\\` | With #772 on top |\n|---|---|---|\n| a clean filter named in \\`.gitattributes\\` | **executed** | not executed, binding \\`unavailable\\` |\n| a filter named only in \\`.git/info/attributes\\` | **executed** | not executed, \\`unavailable\\` |\n| a filter defined in an included file | **executed** | not executed, \\`unavailable\\` |\n| an attributes file named by \\`core.attributesFile\\` | **executed** | not executed, \\`unavailable\\` |\n| \\`core.fsmonitor\\` | not executed (fixed here) | not executed, \\`unavailable\\` |\n\nTwo corrections to my own #772, now pushed there: its first test changed the tracked file's size, and Git then knows a file is modified without reading it, so the filter cases passed without ever triggering a filter; and the included-file fixture was cut at an unquoted \\`;\\`. Both are fixed: with the check disabled the test now fails on \\\"a clean filter: the configured command ran\\\".\n\n#772 is merged up to \\`3600eefd\\`; on that combination \\`audit_export\\` 20/20, \\`audit_command\\` 8/8, \\`audit_bundle\\` 25/25, \\`audit_schema\\` 7/7, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`candidate_git_paths\\` 36/36, \\`tsc\\` clean.\" | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #771 at 3600eefd still REQUEST CHANGES: fsmonitor fixed, but four filter configurations still execute a planted command during audit export (measured; table on the PR). #772 (into Codex's branch) closes them and is merged up to 3600eefd; I corrected two flaws in #772's own test (it had not been triggering the filters). DO NOT MERGE #771 without #772 or an equivalent.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; gh pr view 771 --json state,headRefOid --jq '[.state,.headRefOid[0:8]]|@tsv'; gh pr view 772 --json state,headRefOid --jq '[.state,.headRefOid[0:8]]|@tsv'","description":"Commit and push the test fixes, post the measured results on PR 771, log them, and re-read both PRs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_read_input_tokens":725335,"output_tokens":1321,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1858,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1321,"cache_read_input_tokens":725335,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1858},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":n