{"parentUuid":"28fcf7a2-b184-4d3f-b608-ed71993811e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMKFERmk6pnRxGpP8JJ8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HurMqMBv3gpdq1Z6mbsMNb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/memory/v130-progress.md <<'EOF'\n\n- 2026-11-24 ~07:10Z: #771 (audit candidate binding, Codex) REQUEST CHANGES three times: `audit export` runs git in the recorded workspace and repository-defined filters execute (measured). Codex fixed only fsmonitor (3600eefd). My fix is #772, a PR INTO Codex's branch (check in audit_export.ts: repo-scope git config naming programs → binding `unavailable`); not merged by me. Lesson (mine): my first hostile test changed file size, so git never re-hashed and the filter cases were vacuous; a test for \"X must not run\" has to be shown to fail with the guard removed AND for the right reason (read the failure message). Also twice today `git checkout <file>` to undo a mutation wiped my uncommitted change: commit (or copy the file) before mutating.\nEOF","description":"Record the state and the lessons in the progress notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1559,"cache_read_input_tokens":727193,"output_tokens":407,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1559,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":727193,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1559},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_m