{"parentUuid":"6b5f2be0-c8a8-48d8-914c-201384bb2650","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2aaf70d5-9385-4000-bcb0-a0f51df1e6c5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Em8P9bJiBcCYhXXgcyuJNg","type":"tool_result","content":"-**Candidate-binding slice in progress (branch `codex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding`, based on release `5abbc4c`):** `nexus audit export` now adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. Automated tests for matching, post-validation mutation, unavailable workspace identity, and receipt truncation are written. The TypeScript build passes. Focused tests are **not yet run** because the shared `SUITE` claim is held by a full `make test` process in the context-maturity worktree. Verifier, environment, and acceptance-policy identity remain unimplemented, so WP-P10-03 is still incomplete.\n+**Candidate-binding slice (PR #771, branch `codex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding`):** `nexus audit export` adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. The added `git ls-files` invocation disables `core.fsmonitor`, preventing a repository-configured monitor from running if local Git configuration changes after the audit-export preflight. Local verification passed: `audit_export.test.ts` 19/19, `candidate_git_paths.test.ts` 36/36, and the TypeScript build. Required hosted checks passed at code head `3600eef`; a docs-only update still requires exact-head CI before integration.\n+**Stacked Git-configuration follow-up (PR #772, branch `v1/audit-binding-refuse-repo-programs`):** Audit export lists repository-scoped Git settings that name executable programs or redirect Git behavior and marks receipt binding unavailable when any are present or the listing fails. Its five adversarial configurations are tested with a same-size tracked-file re-hash. The negative control without the preflight executes the planted clean filter and fails the marker assertion. Local verification passed on Node 24: `audit_export` 20/20, `audit_command` 8/8, `audit_bundle` 25/25, `audit_schema` 7/7, `leak_guard` 6/6, `candidate_git_paths` 36/36, and `tsc --noEmit`. Required hosted checks pass on the current stacked head; `Entire Gates` remains pending and is not a required merge check under repository guidance. Both PRs remain open and unmerged.\n+Verifier definition, explicit source-revision/environment identity, and acceptance-policy identity remain unimplemented, so WP-P10-03 is still incomplete.\nlinux-x86_64\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mik\ntest-gates (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/\ntest-gates (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/\ntest-shard (22, 1)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.c\ntest-shard (22, 2)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.c\ntest-shard (22, 3)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.c\ntest-shard (22, 4)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.c\ntest-shard (24, 1)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.c\nt