or size (otherwise git does not re-hash and no filter runs); THEN plant the configuration by writing files directly or with `git config` (after planting, run NO other git command in that repo yourself: your own command would execute the planted program — for `core.fsmonitor` even `git config` is safe but `git status`/`ls-files` are not); the planted command is `sh -c 'echo ran > <marker>; cat'` for filters (it must pass stdin through) and `sh -c 'echo ran > <marker>'` for non-filter programs; marker path is inside the subject's temp root; assert before the export that the marker does not exist yet (print `PLANT-RAN` if it does and skip the case).\n\nCases (each in a fresh `savedSubject({ flight: false })`):\n 1. clean filter via `.gitattributes` + `filter.p.clean` in `.git/config`\n 2. `filter.p.process` (use a command that writes the marker and exits; git will error — that is fine)\n 3. `core.fsmonitor=<cmd>` in `.git/config`\n 4. `include.path` → file under `.git/` defining `[filter \"p\"] clean = \"<cmd>\"` (quote the value: an unquoted `;` starts a comment) + `.gitattributes`\n 5. `includeIf \"gitdir:<abs path of .git>/\"` → same included file + `.gitattributes`\n 6. `core.attributesFile` → a file naming the filter, + `filter.p.clean`\n 7. `.git/info/attributes` naming the filter, + `filter.p.clean`\n 8. move `.git` to a sibling directory `<root>/elsewhere.git`, write a `.git` FILE containing `gitdir: <abs path>`, set `core.worktree` in that config to the workspace, + filter + `.gitattributes`\n 9. `core.worktree = <workspace abs path>` in `.git/config` + filter + `.gitattributes`\n 10. `extensions.worktreeConfig=true` and the filter defined in `.git/config.worktree` + `.gitattributes`\n 11. key-case variants: write `[core]\\n\\tfsMonitor = <cmd>` literally into `.git/config`\n 12. parser desync: append literally to `.git/config` a section whose subsection contains a newline and scope-looking text, e.g. `[filter \"x\\nglobal\\0y\"]`-style attempts — try at least: `[filter \"a\\\\nglobal\"]\\n\\tclean = \"<cmd>\"` (git config escapes: inside the quoted subsection `\\\\n` is not an escape; also try a real newline is not allowed) and a VALUE containing a newline via `clean = \"<cmd>\\\\nglobal\"`; plus `.gitattributes` `* filter=a\\\\nglobal` is unlikely to match — the point is only whether the check still reports `unavailable`. Print the raw result.\n 13. a plain hook FILE with no config key: `.git/hooks/post-index-change` (executable, writes the marker)\n 14. a registered submodule: create a second repo `<root>/sub-src` with a commit, `git -c protocol.file.allow=always submodule add <path> sub` in the workspace and commit (do this BEFORE the mtime bump/plant), then plant in `.git/modules/sub/config` a `filter.p.clean` and in `sub/.gitattributes` `* filter=p`, bump mtime of a tracked file inside `sub/` (same size/content)\n 15. control A (must be allowed): no planted config at all → expect binding `mismatch` (the receipt id is fake) and not executed\n 16. control B (operator's global filter must be allowed): write `$HOME/.gitconfig` in the throwaway HOME with `[filter \"g\"] clean = \"sh -c 'echo ran > <marker>; cat'\"`, `.gitattributes` `* filter=g` in the workspace → expected: EXECUTED is acceptable here (it is the operator's own config) and binding should be `mismatch`, not `unavailable`. Note: the test process's HOME is what git reads, so set `process.env.HOME` handling consistent with how you launch the test (launch with `HOME=<tmp>` and write `<tmp>/.gitconfig` from inside the test using `process.env.HOME`).\n 17. control C: a repo with `filter.lfs.clean = git-lfs clean -- %f` style key in `.git/config` but NO `.gitattributes` using it → expect `unavailable` with the reason (documented trade-off) and not executed.\n\nThen run ONCE: `cd ~/nexus-wt/probe772/cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 500 node --import tsx --test test/zz_probe.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"RESULT|PLANT-RAN|^ℹ (pass|fail)\"`. If the file fails to compile or a helper is missing, fix your probe and rerun (at most three attempts). Then, as a negative control so we know the cases really trigger: temporarily copy `~/nexus-wt/probe772/cli/src/audit_export.ts` aside, edit the worktree copy so the line `if (repositoryConfiguresPrograms(workspacePath)) throw …` never fires (prefix the condition with `false &&`), rerun the same command, save the output, and restore the file from your copy (do NOT use `git checkout` to restore). \n\nRules: do not edit anything outside `~/nexus-wt/probe772` and a scratch dir; no commits, pushes, or GitHub comments; never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus, ~/.config/nexus or ~/.gitconfig; no network; stop any process you start by its own pid, never `pkill -f`; no background loops; shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops; output is filtered by a tool called rtk: prefix a command with `rtk proxy` if its output looks odd). At the end: delete `zz_probe.test.ts`, then `git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/probe772`. Budget: about 30 minutes. If you run out, report what you have rather than nothing.\n\nReport (under 450 words): the tip SHA tested; a table with one row per case: with the check (executed? binding, reason) and with the check disabled (executed? binding); then a plain list of (a) cases where a planted program EXECUTED with the check enabled (these are bypasses — say exactly which), (b) cases that did not trigger even with the check disabled (so they prove nothing), (c) whether the controls behaved as expected; and what you could not run.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ad7fea4d7926ff2ab.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d68ac9ac-5f50-446b-a238-cc2d85cb2c00","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
