{"parentUuid":"09d6c247-332e-4b5a-8254-18e2776dbcde","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMUWVqBaQdhvtjpB9rzU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0164GS4frTZ8fbwrrxH3wQDB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement VR-2 follow-ups","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Implement the six open review follow-ups of unit VR-2 in the Nexus Code CLI. Work ONLY in the git worktree `/home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2f` (branch `v1/vr2-followups`, cut from `origin/release/v1.3.0`). Do not commit, push, open PRs, or touch any other worktree or `~/nexus-code` itself. Do not ask questions; where a detail is open choose the conservative option and list it in your report.\n\nBackground: `nexus acp` (Agent Client Protocol server over stdio for an UNTRUSTED client; `cli/src/acp_stdio.ts`, `cli/src/acp/{types,validate,mapping}.ts`, schema `docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v*.schema.json` generated by `cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs`, ledger `docs/protocol/ACP_ADAPTER_VERSIONS.json`, docs `docs/ACP.md`, evidence `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md`) has an extension method `_nexus/verify` that calls the shared `VerifyService` (`cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`) and returns a verdict and receipt id; receipts are read with `_nexus/receipt/get`. Design plan: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/VR2_PLAN.md` (sections 2, 3 and \"Decisions taken\"). Read the ACP verify code first (`grep -n \"_nexus/verify\\|latestReceipts\\|pinBase\\|verify\" cli/src/acp_stdio.ts`).\n\nFix these, each with tests:\n\n1. Base pin per workspace, not per session. Today the base commit is pinned in `startSession` for every new or loaded session, so a client can commit weakened tests, open a NEW session on the same directory, and be judged against a base that already contains them. Pin once per canonical workspace path for the lifetime of the `nexus acp` process: the first session on a directory pins `HEAD`; every later session (new or load) on that same canonical directory reuses that pin. The map must not grow without bound from client-chosen cwds: cap it (a small multiple of `ACP_MAX_SESSIONS`); beyond the cap, `_nexus/verify` for a not-yet-pinned workspace is refused with a clear error — never silently re-pin or evict a pin. Test: session A on dir D pins B0; make a commit in D; session B on D still uses B0 (assert via the base passed to the service / the receipt's base).\n\n2. The `_nexus/verify` result must name what was covered: add the canonical workspace path and the pinned base commit to the result summary (the receipt already carries `workspace` and `base_pinned_at`). Update types, validation/mapping, regenerate the ACP schema with the generator and make its `--check` mode pass; follow the repo's versioning rule for the ACP adapter schema (look at how v2 and v3 were added in `ACP_ADAPTER_VERSIONS.json` and `cli/test/acp_schema.test.ts`: earlier versions' files must stay byte-identical; add a new version if the result shape changes).\n\n3. Id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` must return TURN receipts only (plan decision 7: existing clients see no change). Today `latestReceipts` mixes verification receipts in, and a test asserts that. Keep verification receipts readable only by explicit id, bound to the session. Update the test: after a `_nexus/verify`, id-less get still returns the last turn receipt (or the existing \"not available\" error when there is none) and get-by-id returns the verification receipt.\n\n4. Interlock tests (a mutation showed they are untested): `_nexus/verify` while a prompt is running on that session is refused and nothing runs; `_nexus/verify` while the session is `stopping` is refused; `session/prompt` while a verification is running is refused; `_nexus/verify` in read-only mode is refused with no receipt; a cross-session receipt read uses a SECOND REAL ACTIVE session on the same connection and must fail. Confirm by mutation that removing the verify-during-prompt check fails a test (copy the source file aside and restore it from the copy — do not use `git checkout` to undo a mutation while you have uncommitted work).\n\n5. Shutdown bound: `ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS` (10 s) equals the verify kill grace, so on a signal the process can exit before a running verification's worker has cleaned up. While a verification is running, the signal deadline must be at least the verify kill grace + 5 s (see what `McpServer.startStdio` in `cli/src/mcp.ts` does). Keep the existing stop semantics in `runAcpStdio`; only lengthen the bound when a verification is in flight. Add a test if cheap (there is a `shutdownGraceMs` option and existing signal tests in `cli/test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts`); otherwise say it is untested.\n\n6. `_meta` on `_nexus/verify`: make it consistent with how the adapter treats `_meta` on its other methods (check `cli/src/acp/validate.ts`) and state the behaviour in `docs/ACP.md`.\n\nDocs, honestly, in `docs/ACP.md` (the `_nexus/verify` section) and `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md`: the client chooses the directory a session works in, so a verification covers that directory; the operator's verifier command and deliverable list are fixed at start-up and applied to the session's directory (read `cli/src/config.ts` near `normalizeTrustedDeliverableFiles` and the worker to describe exactly how deliverables resolve); the result and receipt name the workspace and base; the base is pinned per workspace for the life of the process, so commits made before the first session on that directory are the baseline and restarting `nexus acp` re-pins; the same-user limit described in `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` applies. In the evidence doc replace any test count you cannot reproduce with counts from your own run.\n\nWorking rules (mandatory):\n- Tests: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2f/cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`), one file at a time, foreground. Never read or write the real `~/.nexus`, `/etc/nexus`, `~/.config/nexus`. No live inference, no network.\n- `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .` must be clean. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink; do not run npm install or cargo.\n- New test files import `./helpers/leak_guard.js` first; clear every timer and stop every child you start by its own pid (never `pkill`).\n- Run at the end, one at a time: `acp_stdio`, `acp_validate`, `acp_schema`, `acp_mapping`, `acp_review_fixes`, `acp_client_conformance`, `acp_jsonrpc`, `verify_service`, `leak_guard`, any new test file; `node cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs --check` (or its actual check invocation); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`; `node cli/node_modules/tsx/dist/cli.mjs cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts` from the repo root (a CI gate: listed critical functions must not grow in complexity). Run `acp_stdio` three times in a row to check for flakes.\n- The recorded real-client fixtures in `cli/test/fixtures/acp/clients/` must keep replaying (`acp_client_conformance`).\n- Preserve existing comments and unrelated code. Comments explain why, briefly. Minimum code that meets the spec.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c '...'` for loops; `$PIPESTATUS` is empty in zsh); a hook filters output through `rtk` (prefix with `rtk proxy` if grep/sed output looks odd).\n\nReport (under 450 words): per item: file:line of the change, the tests added, and anything left open; exact test results per file; the mutation result; gates run; deviations and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":755841,"output_tokens":12274,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":652,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_t