he same tarball layout (`scripts/package-linux.sh`, reproducibility check: the package is built twice and compared byte for byte in CI); D13 default = not published.\n\nFor EACH unit give: the acceptance verbatim; what exists that it builds on (file:line); the design (data model, commands/flags, protocol or file formats with exact shapes, state on disk and permissions, lifecycle, failure behaviour, limits); the security analysis; the exact list of files to add/change; the tests by name with what each proves (including hostile cases and, for refactors, the characterization tests that must be green before and after); docs and ledgers; and 2–4 mergeable slices in order, each independently green, with rough size (S/M/L) and the files touched, flagging hot files shared with other work (`cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/src/doctor.ts`, `cli/src/sidecar.ts`, `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, `cli/src/core/run_turn.ts`, `cli/src/config.ts`, `cli/src/types.ts`). Keep each unit to what its acceptance needs and state what is out of scope for v1.3.0. Note dependencies between these units and on BG-1 (detached runs; planned separately: BG-1 may rely on PF-3's socket for live attach) and on GV-1/GV-5 (managed policy; being finished now).\n\nAlso record: a recommended build order across the five units with reasons (smallest and least entangled first; MT-2 is a wide refactor of hot files, so say when it is safest), reference-coding notes per `docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md` (brief; \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" plus what you used is acceptable), risks, and open questions that could not be settled from the code.\n\nShell notes: zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output is filtered by `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` when a grep/sed pipeline looks odd). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus.\n\nReturn (under 600 words): the file path; for each unit the slice list with sizes and hot files; the recommended build order; the decisions taken; the main risks; anything you could not determine. Be concrete enough that an implementer can start slice 1 of each unit from the plan alone.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/acc00870f026d0f74.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b8da9e0-24ea-463d-ad4a-7d9676c51948","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code/cli","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
