{"parentUuid":"464c84d9-ebe8-4c24-bcac-0ed5ac3518cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMUf4Jn64HPH43zwTwZP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build is under way. The first wave is running in parallel, each track in its own worktree.\n\n**Implementing now**\n- **The six VR-2 follow-ups:** the verification base pinned per workspace instead of per session, the result naming the workspace and base, id-less receipt reads returning turn receipts only, tests for the verify/prompt interlocks, the shutdown bound, and `_meta` handling.\n- **GV-1 slices 3–4 and the GV-5 allowlists:** MCP and plugin allowlists enforced, the TUI \"always approve\" gap closed, `sandbox.*` policy reaching `nexus verify`, a `nexus policy check` command, and doctor findings.\n\n**Being planned**\n- BG-1, BG-2 and HK-1 to HK-3 (background runs, hooks, plugins).\n- PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2 and PA-2, with a recommended build order.\n\n**Also running:** the probe of the #772 check on the release branch (seventeen cases, with and without the check).\n\n**How I'm running this**\n- Every unit gets a claim, its own branch, and an independent review before it merges. I've asked the other sessions in the claims log not to merge my PRs before the review is posted.\n- I merge one PR at a time and read the release CI between merges.\n- When every listed item is in and the gates can be evaluated, I'll run the release myself as you directed: version bump and notes, the single merge to `main`, a release candidate first, then the stable tag.\n- BG-3 stays deferred to v1.4, because the plan itself defers it and it wasn't on the list.\n\nI'll report as each track comes back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13870,"cache_read_input_tokens":756493,"output_tokens":539,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13870,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":756493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13870},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMUf43QBcDaGw76MhsZ2","requestRef":"6108e308-0ada-4882-abf9-294c80e78a12","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b0c4daac-7544-4c32-a6bc-6dc1f06a695f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T08:59:00.018Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code/cli","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
