{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:26:53.164Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aae4846fd8cf474b8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0164GS4frTZ8fbwrrxH3wQDB</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/aae4846fd8cf474b8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement VR-2 follow-ups\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All six follow-ups are implemented in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2f`, uncommitted. The one gate that is not clean is `acp_stdio`: two of its existing real-sidecar tests time out on this host, and they do so on unmodified sources too.\n\n**Per item**\n1. **Base pin per workspace** — `cli/src/acp_stdio.ts:248` (`workspaceBase`), cap of 16 at `:55` (`ACP_MAX_PINNED_WORKSPACES = 4 × ACP_MAX_SESSIONS`). Past the cap a new workspace is refused verification; nothing is evicted or re-pinned. Tests: the pin test (new session, symlink alias, loaded session, separate directory) and the bound test.\n2. **Result names coverage** — `cli/src/acp/types.ts:511-515` adds required `workspace`, `base_pinned_commit`, `base_pinned_at`; built at `acp_stdio.ts:448`. Schema is now v4 (`docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v4.schema.json` plus a ledger entry); v1–v3 are byte-identical.\n3. **Id-less receipt get returns turn receipts only** — `acp_stdio.ts:384`. The old assertion in `acp_stdio.test.ts` is rewritten and a new turn-then-verify test added.\n4. **Interlocks** — five tests in the new `cli/test/acp_verify_followups.test.ts`, with the cross-session read using two live sessions.\n5. **Shutdown bound** — `acp_stdio.ts:94` (`shutdownGraceMs()`), used at `:591`: at least kill grace + 5 s while a verification runs. Tested by a unit table and a spawned-process SIGTERM test in `acp_review_fixes.test.ts`.\n6. **`_meta`** — no other validator checks `_meta`, so the shape check on verify is removed (`cli/src/acp/validate.ts`); it is accepted and never read. Stated in `docs/ACP.md`.\n\n**Docs**: `docs/ACP.md` gains a `_nexus/verify` section (it had none), and `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md` is updated with my own counts. I also corrected one sentence in `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` that said the base is pinned per session.\n\n**Mutation**: removing the verify-during-prompt check fails `_nexus/verify is refused while the session's prompt runs and while it is stopping` (7/8). Mutations of the per-workspace pin, the cap, prompt-during-verify, the receipt change and the signal deadline each fail a test too. Every mutation was restored from a copy.\n\n**Results (Node 24.11.1)**\n\n| File | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `acp_verify_followups` | 8/8 |\n| `acp_review_fixes` | 9/9 |\n| `acp_validate` | 15/15 |\n| `acp_schema` | 7/7 |\n| `acp_mapping` | 22/22 |\n| `acp_client_conformance` | 2/2 |\n| `acp_jsonrpc` | 11/11 |\n| `verify_service` | 10/10 |\n| `mcp_verify` | 7/7 |\n| `leak_guard` | 6/6 |\n| `acp_stdio` (9 tests) | first three runs 9/9, 9/9, 8/9; six later runs 8/9 or 7/9 |\n\nThe `acp_stdio` failures are only `ACP stdio completes a sidecar turn…` and `read-only gate refusal stays final…`, both hitting their 10 s wait for a real turn. With HEAD sources swapped back in, the second one failed 6/6 the same way. Host load was 10–13; a probe at a quieter moment showed a turn taking about 4.8 s. I did not establish a cause beyond load.\n\n**Gates**: `tsc` clean, `gen_acp_schema.mjs --check`, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions`, `check_critical_complexity` and `git diff --check` all pass.\n\n**Decisions and open points**\n- A workspace with no commit at its first session keeps that refusal until restart; otherwise commit-then-new-session would choose the base.\n- A failed `session/load` still consumes a pin slot (the pin is taken at session start, as before).\n- The three new fields are on the ACP result only; the shared service summary and the MCP output are unchanged. The receipt carries the base commit only in `result.base`, when verification got that far.\n- The kill grace + 5 s bound mirrors MCP and does not cover the final worker kill at twice the grace.\n- Node 22 and hosted CI were not run.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>196330</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>1769291</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
