{"parentUuid":"e817ca1d-b6b2-4530-9e23-9ba8744a179b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"12485ed9-9c06-4ac6-8f70-4b20f3ec7f2e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ckJNimxB2Ze7KmYoLctSb","type":"tool_result","content":"ready\n   354 /home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/BG_PLAN.md\n   319 /home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md\n   673 total\n12:## 0. What exists (read, with citations)\n30:## 1. Shared design (designed once; the slice that introduces each part is named)\n32:### 1.1 Process model (answers \"what owns a detached run\")\n61:### 1.2 State on disk (introduced in BG-1 slice 1)\n84:### 1.3 Job record `nexus-job` v1 (BG-1 slice 1)\n113:### 1.4 The unattended policy (introduced in BG-1 slice 1 as a pure module, enforced from BG-1 slice 2; BG-2 only adds schedules on top)\n126:### 1.5 Client ↔ runner (BG-1 slice 2): files, not a socket\n132:### 1.6 Identity, liveness, crash, restart and reboot (BG-1 slice 2)\n144:### 1.7 Budgets, deadlines, limits (BG-1 slice 2)\n151:### 1.8 Job receipt `nexus-job-receipt` v1 (BG-1 slice 2; schema + ledger)\n179:## 2. BG-1: commands and behaviour\n198:## 3. BG-2: schedules\n200:### 3.1 What \"schedule\" means in v1.3.0\n204:### 3.2 Schedule record `nexus-schedule` v1 (`R/schedules/<id>.json`)\n236:### 3.3 Commands (in `background_cli.ts`)\n240:## 4. Security analysis\n254:## 5. Files\n262:## 6. Tests (all with a throwaway HOME and `NEXUS_STATE_DIR`, scripted gateway `startGateway` from `cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts`, `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"`, every runner/worker/tool process stopped by pid after a start-ticks check)\n296:## 7. Docs and ledgers\n304:## 8. Slices (each a PR against `release/v1.3.0`, independently green)\n316:## Decisions taken (defaults; no user questions asked)\n330:## Out of scope for v1.3.0\n334:## Reference coding\n338:## Risks\n348:## Open questions that could not be settled from the code","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b13ca8d5-5254-43e6-8791-8477454fb889","timestamp":"2026-1