{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"4befa3b43a31330eff2d7261965fa0a3c495c21e4e3c507c95ce17451445da3a","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PreToolUse:Bash hook additional context: graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context.\n\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae29f643905427be2</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01HhzQA4RwkngLHdFCWgxbFb</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ae29f643905427be2.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PRs #774 and #775\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## PR #774: REQUEST CHANGES at 9e9366d8686ea37437ff26f47e9b67583c462c9a\nThe head had not moved when I finished, and the PR is still open.\n\n**Blocking**\n1. **Stale sidecar schema.** `docs/protocol/sidecar-v1.schema.json` is out of date. The new `TurnResult` fields make `protocol_schema` fail 1 of 8: \"checked-in protocol schema equals a fresh generation\". Running `node cli/scripts/gen_protocol_schema.mjs` adds 12 lines, and `--check` fails. I reverted the regeneration in my worktree. The fix is to regenerate it and record the version decision in `docs/protocol/VERSIONS.json`. I did not check that failure on the base; #775, on a nearby base, passes this test. (confirmed by running)\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- The admission mutation survived. I made `initialTaskTimeStopReason` return `undefined`, and all 6 tests still passed. The loop-top `Date.now() &gt; turnDeadline` check is a backstop, since the timer is not armed at a zero limit. That makes the admission check redundant, and the test at line 78 does not pin it. With a zero limit the backstop uses `&gt;` on the same millisecond, so a step could dispatch. Add a test with a stubbed or frozen clock. (confirmed by running)\n- The reset mutation was caught. Setting `taskElapsedMs = 0` on begin fails the \"can only be lowered on resume\" test (5 pass, 1 fail). (confirmed by running)\n- A backwards clock jump within a process exhausts the whole budget. `finishTaskElapsedBudget` sets elapsed to the maximum whenever now &lt; `taskActiveSinceMs`. This fails closed, but a small NTP step permanently kills a long objective. Consider a monotonic `process.hrtime` delta within one process, and wall clock only across processes. (by reading)\n- Legacy objectives with no counter are charged `now − startedAt`. Any objective older than 3 days (the 4320 min default) is exhausted on its first resume. This is deliberate and conservative, but it should be called out in the docs. (by reading)\n- Idle time between clean turns is not counted. Only running intervals and crash or kill downtime are counted. Any open interval is charged through downtime, so a kill followed by a resume a week later exhausts the budget. The code behaves this way, but I found no operator-facing doc stating it. (by reading)\n- `--no-continuation` leaves `budget` undefined, so there is no task limit. This matches the #762 turn deadline. (by reading)\n- Persisted elapsed time is written once at begin, as `taskActiveSinceMs`, which survives a kill. The reservation is saved before any dispatch, and a failed save blocks inference. (by reading plus a test)\n- The deadline timer is cleared on the catch path and on the normal path. The normal-path clear moved after the compaction drain. A timer firing during that drain is neutralised by `shouldOverrideStopAfterDeadline`. The unified `min(turn, task remaining)` timer avoids two timers. (by reading)\n- The limit is configured by `--max-task-minutes` or `NEXUS_MAX_TASK_MINUTES`. It sits in `PROJECT_ENV_KEYS`, so a project `.env` can set it, as with the submission budget. It can only lower the ceiling, because a resume keeps `min(saved, new)`. It defaults to 4320 and is capped at `MAX_CONTINUATION_MINUTES`. Invalid values throw in `assertValidContinuationBudget`. The docs touch only the plan progress note, and I did not check whether it names the project-`.env` behaviour. (by reading)\n\n**Gates**\n- Complexity: `runTurnImpl` CC 324→324, nesting 5→5. Lines went 1262→1290, and the gate did not complain about that.\n- Samples: `gen_protocol_samples --check` says current.\n- Run-result schema: additive, `schema_version` stays 1, and a ledger entry was appended.\n- Leak guard: imported by the new test file.\n- tsc: clean.\n\n**Tests**\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| p10_task_elapsed_budget | 6 | 0 |\n| leak_guard | 6 | 0 |\n| protocol_parity | 5 | 0 |\n| protocol_schema | 7 | 1 |\n| run_json_contract | 15 | 0 |\n| check_requirements | 28 | 0 |\n| p10_inference_submission_budget | 4 | 0 |\n| turn_deadline_abort | 3 | 0 |\n\n## PR #775: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, but the head moved\nI reviewed af6c50e046ba157d716313ebbe4ed8b62442a22a. The head is now 7945d57b46f4e2e4a27d9d43bc250cef6c60c914, so this verdict does not cover it. I did not review the new commit.\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- **Doc over-claims resume.** The doc says \"Resume continues after the operator raises the cap\". I found no operator path that