{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T10:26:34.950Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab08d468d59756d02</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01284R4pgJy7JFABQT3TK9xb</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ab08d468d59756d02.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement GV-1 slices 3-4 and GV-5\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>A, B and C are implemented and tested in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/gv1c`; D is left marked \"not yet\". Nothing is committed. Two mandated suites did not finish cleanly on this host (load average 10–19): `context_convergence` was cut at 15 minutes and `sidecar` had 8 load-related failures.\n\n**A. Allowlists (GV-5): done**\n- **MCP:** `cli/src/mcp.ts` gates every server before it starts (`policyDescriptor` :131, `refusedByPolicy` :610), covering `loadAndConnect`, `addServer` (`/mcp add` saves nothing when refused) and `addConnection`.\n- **Plugins:** `cli/src/plugins.ts:83` checks real path and SHA-256 before `import()`.\n- **Workspace test:** `isWorkspaceFile` (`cli/src/workspace_trust.ts:36`) counts a file as the workspace's by path or by symlink target.\n- **Reporting and failure:** refusals name the policy source, go to stderr once, and are available via `getPolicyRefusals()`. An unreadable policy admits nothing.\n- **Tests:** `managed_policy_allowlists.test.ts` (18), including the hostile cases you listed.\n\n**B. Slice 3: done, no Rust change (TUI text unchanged)**\n- **\"Always\" answer:** `cli/src/sidecar.ts:900/918` approves the one call and does not remember it.\n- **REPL:** `cli/src/repl.ts:214`. The doc said the REPL \"asks every time\"; in fact `/mode auto` and \"always\" set its own mode copy and it stopped asking. Fixed.\n- **`/mode auto` reply:** `cli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:178` now returns the refusal with its source instead of \"Mode: auto\".\n- **`nexus verify`:** `verifyFlagRefusal` (`cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts:156`, called at `cli/src/index.ts:727`) refuses `--yes`, `--sandbox none` and `--sandbox-network`, exit 2.\n- **Tests:** `managed_policy_always.test.ts` (6), `managed_policy_verify.test.ts` (12).\n- **Left:** the sandbox itself still does not consult `sandbox.forbid_network` (`sandbox.ts`, slice 5); the doc says so.\n\n**C. Slice 4: done except `policy approve`**\n- **Commands:** new `cli/src/policy_cli.ts` with `nexus policy show` and `nexus policy check [file]`, both with `--json`, exit 2 when invalid. They run with a broken policy (`cli/src/index.ts:1562`).\n- **Doctor:** findings `policy.system|user|project|effective` (`cli/src/doctor.ts:1251`); `--fix` skips any `policy.toml` (:1433).\n- **Loader:** `inspectManagedTiers` (`cli/src/core/managed_policy_load.ts:413`) reports both tiers even when the first is broken.\n- **Tests:** `policy_cli.test.ts` (23).\n\n**D.** `egress.secret_destinations` is not assigned to slices 3–4, so it stays \"not yet\".\n\n**Docs:** `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md` and `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` updated; the four new manual commands parse with `--help`. Two guard tests were updated to the new state (`managed_policy_enforcement`, `managed_policy_schema`).\n\n**Test results**\n\n| File | Result |\n|---|---|\n| allowlists, policy_cli, managed_policy_verify | 18/18, 23/23, 12/12, each ×3 |\n| managed_policy_always | 6/6 ×3 |\n| managed_policy_enforcement / schema | 113/113, 57/57 |\n| managed_policy_load / merge / toml / integrity / dispatch / startup | 97, 46, 111, 17, 14, 10, all pass |\n| approval_policy, mcp, mcp_verify | 16/16, 4/4, 7/7 |\n| verify_command, verify_sandbox | 18/18, 10/10 |\n| check_requirements, leak_guard, release_workflow_parity, lsp_shape | 28/28, 6/6, 6/6, 8/8 |\n| doctor | 49 pass, 11 fail; failing set identical to base |\n| sidecar | 57/65; the 8 failures are 10 s wait timeouts and timing assertions |\n| context_convergence | 6 passed, then cut at 15 min (about 70 tests at roughly 2 min each); incomplete |\n\n- **Sidecar follow-up:** on isolated reruns the approval tests pass; \"leaving read-only checkpoint fallback\" also times out on base. The remaining two (`cancel during inference`, `cancelling /tdd`) were not rerun.\n- **Tool descriptions:** none were changed.\n- **Gates:** `tsc` clean; `check_invariants`, `check_requirements`, `check_doc_versions` and the complexity gate pass (all five functions unchanged).\n\n**Release notes**\n- Servers and plugins outside the allowlists no longer start or load.\n- \"Always\" and `/mode auto` are refused under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`.\n- `nexus verify` refuses the three flags above.\n- New `nexus policy show|check`, and four new doctor findings.\n\n**Deviations and conservative choices**\n- `policy approve` is not implemented: it would be a second approval path a model could run; `nexus trust` remains the only one.\n- Bare-name and unnormalized commands never match a `command:` entry; WebSocket servers match by name only.\n- When the workspace is `$HOME`, `disable_workspace` also switches off the user's own MCP config and plugins.\n- A plugin is hashed, then imported by path, so a replace-in-between race remains (documented).\n- XERJ was not queried (no-network rule).\n- Not edited: `CHANGELOG.md` and the GV-1/GV-5 rows of `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md` (now stale).\n- `origin/release/v1.3.0` is one commit ahead of this branch's base.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>344616</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>119</tool_uses><duration_ms>5321590</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
