{"parentUuid":"05666b54-7437-47fd-bb5e-680a8200cdb3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMwCcNUsEt6Ai7ktkzYv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DssjTMvFAHDJWcqqRUERLV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n'''\nnew='''admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n- **A name does not admit a server the workspace configures.** A name is whatever the configuring file says it is, so\n  a repository could reuse an allowed name for a program or a URL of its own. A server defined by a file of the\n  workspace is admitted only by a `command:` or a `url:` entry that matches what it would reach; with only a name entry\n  it is refused, and the message says so. Consequently a WebSocket server can only come from your own configuration.\n  A name entry still admits a server from your user configuration, whatever it runs: a name pins nothing by itself.\n- **What an entry does not pin.** A `command:` entry pins the program and not its arguments. A plugin's `sha256:`\n  entry covers the plugin's entry file and not the modules that file imports. A hard link in your configuration\n  directory to a file of the workspace is treated as your file: `disable_workspace` goes by path and by symbolic\n  link, and a repository cannot create such a link.\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; open(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\ncd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; bash -c 'for f in managed_policy_merge policy_cli managed_policy_allowlists managed_policy_enforcement mcp leak_guard; do TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 280 node --import tsx --test test/$f.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) |^✖ \" | cut -c1-150 | tr \"\\n\" \" \"; echo \"<- $f\"; done'","description":"Document the rule and the limits, then type-check and run the policy tests","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":926702,"output_tokens":829,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":926702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":6479,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DssjTMvFAHDJWcqqRUERLV":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n'''\nnew='''admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n- **A name does not admit a server the workspace configures.** A name is whatever the configuring file says it is, so\n  a repository could reuse an allowed name for a program or a URL of its own. A server defined by a file of the\n  workspace is admitted only by a `command:` or a `url:` entry that matches what it would reach; with only a name entry\n  it is refused, and the message says so. Consequently a WebSocket server can only come from your own configuration.\n  A name entry still admits a server from your user config