{"parentUuid":"da2b3b3d-4408-4edd-8794-b1c43cd8e732","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMwosXHdaiomFEe9qusw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015UvEaLr1MaQGrE1fKEM4Uj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && git add -A cli && git commit -q -m \"fix(policy): cut rejected tokens by pairing quotes in order\n\nThe first version paired the second and third quote of a message such as\n\\\"expected '=' after the key 'x'\\\", cut the fixed text and left the file's\ntoken whole, so a line with no '=' was still read out in full. Quotes are now\ntaken pair by pair; a token is kept only when it is short, is a dotted name\nunder one of the policy's own tables, or is one of the loader's own examples.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1; git push -q origin v1/policy-followups 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/policy-followups | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 783 --body \"**Independent review at \\`ad138d2f\\` — REQUEST CHANGES on the error-text half; fixed in the commit now pushed.**\n\n- **The allowlist change is sound.** \\`fromWorkspace\\` is computed on the one path that reads files (\\`loadAndConnect\\`, through \\`isWorkspaceFile\\`, which also catches symlinks into the workspace). Configurations are not merged field by field: each name's whole entry comes from the first file that defines it, so there is no entry with a user's name and a workspace's command. A refused workspace entry falls through to the user's own entry of that name. \\`addServer\\` and \\`addConnection\\` pass \\`false\\`; their callers are the operator's \\`/mcp add\\` and the REPL wizard. A workspace server with a bare command such as \\`npx\\` has no pinnable path and is now refused with the new message, as the document says. Removing the rule fails the new test.\n- **The error-text cut did not work** (confirmed by running): the pattern paired the second and third quote of \\`expected '=' after the key '<key>'\\`, cut the fixed text and left the file's token whole. A line with no \\`=\\` was echoed in full, a 5,000-character line gave a 5,031-character error, and \\`--json\\` carried the same.\n\n**Fix:** quotes are now taken pair by pair, in order. A quoted token is kept only when it is shorter than nine characters, is a dotted lower-case name under one of the policy's own tables (what a mistyped key looks like), or is one of the loader's own examples (\\`command:/absolute/path\\` and the like). The test now includes the reviewer's two cases. What the check prints for five crafted files:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nline 2: expected '=' after the key 'dbpasswo…'\nline 3: unsupported value 'sk-live-…': expected a \\\"string\\\", true, false, a whole number or an array of strings\nline 3: key 'mcp.allow', item 1 (\\\"has spac…\\\") must be a server name (…), \\\"command:/absolute/path\\\" or \\\"url:https://origin\\\"\nline 3: unknown key 'approval.mysecretlowercasetoken'\nline 3: unknown key 'approval.strictt'\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThe fourth line is the remaining limit: a lower-case name under a real policy table is shown in full, because that is exactly what a mistyped key is.\n\nTests after the fix: \\`policy_cli\\` 24/24, \\`managed_policy_merge\\` 47/47, \\`managed_policy_toml\\` 111/111, \\`managed_policy_load\\` 97/97, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`tsc\\` clean. Not checked by the reviewer: whether model-originated text can reach \\`/mcp add\\`.\" | tail -1","description":"Commit and push the corrected error-text cut and post the review and fix on PR 783"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4436,"cache_read_input_tokens":945849,"output_tokens":1495,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":55},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4436,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1495,"cache_read_input_tokens":945849,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4436},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9996,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015UvEaLr1MaQGrE1fKEM4Uj":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && git add -A cli && git commit -q -m \"fix(policy): cut rejected tokens by pairing quotes in order\n\nThe first version paired the second and third quote of a message such as\n\\\"expected '=' after the key 'x'\\\", cut the fixed text and left the file's\ntoken whole, so a line with no '=' was still read out in full. Quotes are now\ntaken pair by pair; a token is kept only when it is short, is a dotted name\nunder one of the policy's own tables, or is one of the loader's own examples.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1; git push -q origin v1/policy-followups 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/policy-followups | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 783 --body \"**Independent review at \\`ad138d2f\\` — REQUEST CHANGES on the error-text half; fixed in the commit now pushed.**\n\n- **The allowlist change is sound.** \\`fromWorkspace\\` is computed on the one path that reads files (\\`loadAndConnect\\`, through \\`isWorkspaceFile\\`, which also catches symlinks into the workspace). Configurations are not merged field by field: each name's whole entry comes from the first file that defines it, so there is no entry with a user's name and a workspace's command. A refused workspace entry falls through to the user's own entry of that name. \\`addServer\\` and \\`addConnection\\` pass \\`false\\`; their callers are the operator's \\`/mcp add\\` and the REPL wizard. A workspace server with a bare command such as \\`npx\\` has no pinnable path and is now refused with the new message, as the document says. Removing the rule fails the new test.\n- **The error-text cut did not work** (confirmed by running): the pattern paired the second and third quote of \\`expected '=' after the key '<key>'\\`, cut the fixed text and left the file's token whole. A line with no \\`=\\` was echoed in full, a 5,000-character line gave a 5,031-character error, and \\`--json\\` carried the same.\n\n**Fix:** quotes are now taken pair by pair, in order. A quoted token is kept only when it is shorter than nine characters, is a dotted lower-case name under one of the policy's own tables (what a mistyped key looks like), or is one of the loader's own examples (\\`command:/absolute/path\\` and the like). The test now includes the reviewer's two cases. What the check prints for five crafted files:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nline 2: expected '=' after the key 'dbpasswo…'\nline 3: unsupported value 'sk-live-…': expected a \\\"string\\\", true, false, a whole number or an array of strings\nline 3: key 'mcp.allow', item 1 (\\\"has spac…\\\") must be a server name (…), \\\"command:/absolute/path\\\" or \\\"url:https://origin\\\"\nline 3: unknown key 'approval.mysecretlowercasetoken'\nline 3: unknown key 'approval.strictt'\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThe fourth line is the remaining limit: a lower-case name under a real policy table is shown in full, because that is exactly what a mistyped key is.\n\nTests after the fix: \\`policy_cli\\` 24/24, \\`managed_policy_merge\\` 47/47, \\`managed_policy_toml\\` 111/111, \\`managed_policy_load\\` 97/97, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`tsc\\` clean. Not checked by the reviewer: whether model-originated text can reach \\`/mcp add\\`.\" | tail -1","description":"Commit and push the corrected error-text cut and post the review and fix on PR 783"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChMwosFQgHRFAjRpQ9Nat","requestRef":"37466094-f5fb-4b5a-a4fd-8eecede5b4ca","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d1163a0-81da-484d-bedd-bbbb992a245c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:55:11.577Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
