{"parentUuid":"984a26e0-9cf4-4bca-a3a7-7dda4b258dca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMwtHSZFeNhYbjAjw152","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1581,"cache_read_input_tokens":950285,"output_tokens":2536,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":406},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1581,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2536,"cache_read_input_tokens":950285,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1581},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4280,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMwtH7yBdtVLuDYxYeAb","requestRef":"72f8ae31-8335-4f46-82ec-a2f268ab1db4","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"82e989da-4c53-4dbf-a4a4-4b2da624f17d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:56:03.129Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"82e989da-4c53-4dbf-a4a4-4b2da624f17d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMwtHSZFeNhYbjAjw152","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HzoTpGGCvxPdxpVMdJwggw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md","content":"**Independent review at `034c278cad62e7e849c4b68037d2ef32b2801af5` — REQUEST CHANGES. The hook output handling and the gate ordering hold; all three blockers are about who can get a hook trusted. I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking, each confirmed by running**\n\n1. **The model can approve its own project hooks.** `nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hex>` works with no terminal (`hooks_cli.ts`, about line 118), and neither the trust store (`extension_trust.json`) nor `hooks.json` is in `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` (`security.ts:163`), unlike `policy_trust.json` and `trusted_workspaces.json`. In auto mode: `write_file .nexus/hooks.json`, then `run_command \"nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hash> -w <repo>\"` exited 0, wrote the store, and the hook ran on the next call. (Unsandboxed `run_command` sees `~/.config/nexus`; with `--sandbox` the home directory is masked; in review mode the operator would see the command.)\n2. **With the workspace set to the home directory, the model can write an active operator hooks file.** `write_file .config/nexus/hooks.json` succeeded; at umask 022 the file is mode 644, which the mode check accepts, and the \"operator\" hook ran with no approval. At umask 002 the file is rejected and every call is denied instead.\n3. **Approval does not pin the script a hook names.** After approving `command: [\"./guard.sh\"]`, the model overwrote `guard.sh` and the next call ran the model's script with the operator's rights, outside the sandbox, with no new approval. `docs/HOOKS.md` says the approval is for \"the file's exact bytes\" and never says this.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- A hook's denial reason reaches the model as `[hook X (project)] <up to 1000 chars>`: one line, named and sourced, but not marked as untrusted text, so an instruction in it passes through. It should be quoted as hook-supplied text. (Plain stdout and the receipt's hook summaries do not reach the model.)\n- A running hook is not stopped by cancel or by the turn deadline, and time spent queued behind another hook is outside its 120 s budget. The document says the first.\n- `HOOKS.md` claims subagents and operation units are covered. Subagents are (same dispatch and spine). Operation units get their own agent on another workspace path, so project hooks do not run there; no test covers either.\n- The hooks stage also gates the operator's own `!cmd`; undocumented.\n- When a hook denies a call that a spine-stage gate (read-only, workspace boundary, grants) would have denied, the gate's reason and anything the later stages would have recorded (sandbox-denial events) are replaced by `HOOK_DENIED`. A hook-denied call is still charged to the tool-invocation budget.\n\n**Held up**\n\n- Nineteen output shapes fed to the reducer (duplicate keys, a BOM, `continue` as a string, null and array decisions, a deny mixed with an allow, exit codes 1, 3 and 126, stderr only): none admitted anything, and every unreadable or unknown shape denied.\n- A `post-tool` hook only reads the receipt. The move of helpers out of `verify_service.ts` is verbatim (`verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7).\n- Mutations, each caught: an allow that skips the authority stage; a hook error that continues; skipping the project hash check (6 failures); passing the full environment.\n\n**Tests at this head, 0 failures:** the thirteen hook files (101 tests), `approval_policy` 16, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `hash_chain` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate and `check_invariants` pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the approve command under `--sandbox` in production form; a hook stalling a turn past its deadline (read only); the doctor output for an invalid operator file beyond its test; the schema and examples.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1581,"cache_read_input_tokens":950285,"output_tokens":2536,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":406},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1581,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2536,"cache_read_input_tokens":950285,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1581},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13049,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HzoTpGGCvxPdxpVMdJwggw":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md","content":"**Independent review at `034c278cad62e7e849c4b68037d2ef32b2801af5` — REQUEST CHANGES. The hook output handling and the gate ordering hold; all three blockers are about who can get a hook trusted. I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking, each confirmed by running**\n\n1. **The model can approve its own project hooks.** `nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hex>` works with no terminal (`hooks_cli.ts`, about line 118), and neither the trust store (`extension_trust.json`) nor `hooks.json` is in `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` (`security.ts:163`), unlike `policy_trust.json` and `trusted_workspaces.json`. In auto mode: `write_file .nexus/hooks.json`, then `run_command \"nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hash> -w <repo>\"` exited 0, wrote the store, and the hook ran on the next call. (Unsandboxed `run_command` sees `~/.config/nexus`; with `--sandbox` the home directory is masked; in review mode the operator would see the command.)\n2. **With the workspace set to the home directory, the model can write an active operator hooks file.** `write_file .config/nexus/hooks.json` succeeded; at umask 022 the file is mode 644, which the mode check accepts, and the \"operator\" hook ran with no approval. At umask 002 the file is rejected and every call is denied instead.\n3. **Approval does not pin the script a hook names.** After approving `command: [\"./guard.sh\"]`, the model overwrote `guard.sh` and the next call ran the model's script with the operator's rights, outside the sandbox, with no new approval. `docs/HOOKS.md` says the approval is for \"the file's exact bytes\" and never says this.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- A hook's denial reason reaches the model as `[hook X (project)] <up to 1000 chars>`: one line, named and sourced, but not marked as untrusted text, so an instruction in it passes through. It should be quoted as hook-supplied text. (Plain stdout and the receipt's hook summaries do not reach the model.)\n- A running hook is not stopped by cancel or by the turn deadline, and time spent queued behind another hook is outside its 120 s budget. The document says the first.\n- `HOOKS.md` claims subagents and operation units are covered. Subagents are (same dispatch and spine). Operation units get their own agent on another workspace path, so project hooks do not run there; no test covers either.\n- The hooks stage also gates the operator's own `!cmd`; undocumented.\n- When a hook denies a call that a spine-stage gate (read-only, workspace boundary, grants) would have denied, the gate's reason and anything the later stages would have recorded (sandbox-denial events) are replaced by `HOOK_DENIED`. A hook-denied call is still charged to the tool-invocation budget.\n\n**Held up**\n\n- Nineteen output shapes fed to the reducer (duplicate keys, a BOM, `continue` as a string, null and array decisions, a deny mixed with an allow, exit codes 1, 3 and 126, stderr only): none admitted anything, and every unreadable or unknown shape denied.\n- A `post-tool` hook only reads the receipt. The move of helpers out of `verify_service.ts` is verbatim (`verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7).\n- Mutations, each caught: an allow that skips the authority stage; a hook error that continues; skipping the project hash check (6 failures); passing the full environment.\n\n**Tests at this head, 0 failures:** the thirteen hook files (101 tests), `approval_policy` 16, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `hash_chain` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate and `check_invariants` pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the approve command under `--sandbox` in production form; a hook stalling a turn past its deadline (read only); the doctor output for an invalid operator file beyond its test; the schema and examples.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChMwtH7yBdtVLuDYxYeAb","requestRef":"72f8ae31-8335-4f46-82ec-a2f268ab1db4","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"0473986d-1ec8-4472-92d8-50ee86fb237c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:56:16.197Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
