{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"ee09ae7bae4c8ae95be0988182973e354f4a4b9cb210ee8370e6a58ddd16000b","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MLJi7jnv66KS41Gj51qsoP","type":"tool_result","content":"    assert.deepEqual(clampSandboxNetwork(required, true, origin), {\n      allowed: false,\n      message: `${origin} is refused: managed policy forbids network access in the sandbox. [policy: system /fake/etc/nexus/policy.toml sandbox.forbid_network]`,\n      source: { tier: \"system\", file: SYS, key: \"sandbox.forbid_network\" },\n    });\n  }\n  assert.deepEqual(clampSandboxNetwork(required, false, \"default\"), { allowed: true, value: false, source: { tier: \"system\", file: SYS, key: \"sandbox.forbid_network\" } });\n  assert.deepEqual(clampSandboxNetwork(NONE, true, \"--sandbox-network\"), { allowed: true, value: true, source: { tier: \"default\", key: \"sandbox.forbid_network\" } });\n});\n\ntest(\"an MCP server outside mcp.allow is refused; a workspace server is refused under disable_workspace\", () => {\n  const policy = sys({ mcp: { allow: [\"github\", \"command:/usr/local/bin/mcp-files\", \"url:https://mcp.example.com\"], disable_workspace: true } });\n  const source = { tier: \"system\", file: SYS, key: \"mcp.allow\" };\n  assert.deepEqual(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"shell\", command: \"/usr/bin/evil\", fromWorkspace: false }), {\n    allowed: false,\n    message: \"MCP server 'shell' is not started: it is not in the managed allowlist (mcp.allow). [policy: system /fake/etc/nexus/policy.toml mcp.allow]\",\n    source,\n  });\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"github\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"anything\", command: \"/usr/local/bin/mcp-files\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"remote\", url: \"https://mcp.example.com/sse?x=1\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\n  assert.ok(!permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"remote\", url: \"https://mcp.example.com.evil.test/sse\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\n  assert.ok(!permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"remote\", url: \"http://mcp.example.com/sse\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed, \"another scheme is another origin\");\n  assert.ok(!permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"remote\", url: \"not a url\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\n  assert.ok(!permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"x\", command: \"/usr/local/bin/mcp-files-2\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"3c549e03b657e73811328822a297408798db46a7d7fa5edac07c7144edb1dc18","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RTHMGkV7gy62GvXTkjGcUJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='cli/test/managed_policy_merge.test.ts'; s=open(p).read()\nanchor='test(\"an MCP server outside mcp.allow is refused; a workspace server is refused under disable_workspace\", () => {'\nnew='''test(\"a name in mcp.allow does not admit a server the workspace configures: the repository would choose what runs behind the name\", () => {\n  const policy = sys({ mcp: { allow: [\"files\", \"command:/usr/local/bin/mcp-files\", \"url:https://mcp.example.com\"] } });\n  // The operator's own definition of the name is admitted, whatever it runs.\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"files\", command: \"/opt/tools/files\", fromWorkspace: false }).allowed);\n  // A workspace file that reuses the name with its own program or URL is not.\n  for (const planted of [{ command: \"/workspace/evil\" }, { url: \"https://attacker.example/sse\" }, {}]) {\n    const decision = permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"files\", ...planted, fromWorkspace: true });\n    assert.equal(decision.allowed, false, JSON.stringify(planted));\n    assert.match((decision as { message: string }).message, /a name does not admit a server that the workspace configures\\\\. List its program \\\\(command:\\\\) or its URL \\\\(url:\\\\)\\\\./);\n  }\n  // What a workspace definition would reach still admits it.\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"whatever\", command: \"/usr/local/bin/mcp-files\", fromWorkspace: true }).allowed);\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(policy, { name: \"files\", url: \"https://mcp.example.com/sse\", fromWorkspace: true }).allowed);\n  // With no allowlist nothing changes for workspace servers.\n  assert.ok(permitsMcpServer(NONE, { name: \"files\", command: \"/workspace/anything\", fromWorkspace: true }).allowed);\n});\n\n'''\nassert s.count(anchor)==1; open(p,'w').write(s.replace(anchor,new+anchor))\nEOF\nrtk proxy grep -n \"name entry\\|only a name\\|mcp.allow\" docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md | cut -c1-240 | head -8","description":"Add a test for the name-entry rule and find the doc text to correct"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"3c12061f2667c68ae058498286d6a460b0c17312fbdbaf3c0038b29255a74204","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTHMGkV7gy62GvXTkjGcUJ","type":"tool_result","content":"32:| `mcp.allow` | yes | A configured server is checked before it is started: one that no entry admits is not started, in `nexus mcp`, in a session and for `/mcp add` (which then saves nothing). See \"MCP servers and plugins\" below. |\n33:| `mcp.disable_workspace` | yes | A server configured by a file of the workspace is not started, whether or not the workspace is trusted and whatever `mcp.allow` says. |\n45:  `nexus: MCP server 'shell' is not started: it is not in the managed allowlist (mcp.allow). [policy: system\n46:  /etc/nexus/policy.toml mcp.allow]`. The session continues without it.\n47:- **How a server is matched.** A bare name entry matches the server's configured name, character for character:\n53:  admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n179:| `mcp.allow` | allowlist | intersection | The only MCP servers that may start. An entry is a server name, `\"command:/absolute/path\"` or `\"url:https://origin\"`. |\n373:line 5: key 'mcp.allow', item 2 (\"cmd:/x\") must be a server name (letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'), \"command:/absolute/path\" or \"url:https://origin\"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"ac4d262418e00987f951e2f5e50d2a2c22c62ce045ff7f3f66c253c56a4fc0d2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016X9CSRmwNYMRgyTZbK5DiY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && sed -n 47,56p docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md | cut -c1-400","description":"Read the matching paragraph in the policy doc"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"f2e910b302e3f5265f131763b8429efabd74da1a5e52fd4b7083986fb43f231f","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016X9CSRmwNYMRgyTZbK5DiY","type":"tool_result","content":"- **How a server is matched.** A bare name entry matches the server's configured name, character for character:\n  `github` does not admit `GitHub` or `github ` (with a space). A `command:` entry matches a stdio server whose\n  configured `command` is exactly that absolute path; a command given as a bare name (`npx`, found through `PATH`)\n  or as a path that is not normalized is never matched by a `command:` entry. A `command:` entry pins the program,\n  not its arguments: `command:/usr/bin/node` admits any script run by that Node. A `url:` entry matches a remote\n  server (SSE or HTTP transport) whose URL has exactly that origin; a definition that would run a program is never\n  admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n- **How a plugin is matched.** By the file, because a plugin's name is known only after its code ran: a `sha256:`\n  entry matches the SHA-256 of the file's bytes, a `file:` entry the file's real path (a symbolic link is resolved\nShell cwd was reset to /home/mike/nexus-code","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"22c15bce74603a0e01b5621d11721c047b6be0f52286916b5e45544faf0b4b1f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DssjTMvFAHDJWcqqRUERLV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n'''\nnew='''admitted by a `url` it also carries. A WebSocket server (`ws://`, `wss://`) has no `http(s)` origin, so only a name\n  entry admits it.\n- **A name does not admit a server the workspace configures.** A name is whatever the configuring file says it is, so\n  a repository could reuse an allowed name for a program or a URL of its own. A server defined by a file of the\n  workspace is admitted only by a `command:` or a `url:` entry that matches what it would reach; with only a name entry\n  it is refused, and the message says so. Consequently a WebSocket server can only come from your own configuration.\n  A name entry still admits a server from your user configuration, whatever it runs: a name pins nothing by itself.\n- **What an entry does not pin.** A `command:` entry pins the program and not its arguments. A plugin's `sha256:`\n  entry covers the plugin's entry file and not the modules that file imports. A hard link in your configuration\n  directory to a file of the workspace is treated as your file: `disable_workspace` goes by path and by symbolic\n  link, and a repository cannot create such a link.\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; open(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\ncd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; bash -c 'for f in managed_policy_merge policy_cli managed_policy_allowlists managed_policy_enforcement mcp leak_guard; do TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 280 node --import tsx --test test/$f.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) |^✖ \" | cut -c1-150 | tr \"\\n\" \" \"; echo \"<- $f\"; done'","description":"Document the rule and the limits, then type-check and run the policy tests","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
