{"parentUuid":"40a344c0-fba4-4c74-b22b-0731f76c0d48","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMxi7TsyL5AGSpcxoV6W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#783 (the policy follow-ups) is merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `96e8f24f`; release CI on that commit is still running, so the branch is not confirmed green yet.\n\n- **#783:** its review asked for changes on the error-text half, because my first cut still echoed a whole line that had no `=`. I fixed that and re-ran the policy tests; the fix commit itself was not re-read by a second reviewer before I merged.\n- **#782 (my HK-1 hooks):** review came back request changes with three blockers, all confirmed by running. The fixes are being made on the branch now; it stays unmerged until they are in and re-reviewed.\n  - The model can approve its own project hooks.\n  - With the workspace set to the home directory, it can write an active operator hooks file.\n  - Approving a hook does not pin the script it names.\n- **#779 (Codex's PF-4):** review posted as request changes. The library is sound, but its example and docs snippet approve any verifier request, including ones the model declares.\n- **#780 (Codex's BG-1):** still red on both test-matrix checks.\n- **PA-2:** build still running.\n- **MT-2:** claimed and started with slice 1, characterization tests only, no source changes.\n\nBG-2, HK-2, HK-3 and PF-3 are not started. Next I read the release CI result for `96e8f24f`, then act on the hooks fixes and the PA-2 and MT-2 builds as they report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3055,"cache_read_input_tokens":136398,"output_tokens":479,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":479,"cache_read_input_tokens":136398,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3055},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMxi7DzoV9fjF5oH8k44","requestRef":"876e0ce4-d30b-4925-8929-4790f46493a7","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d1b27feb-fb67-446c-a860-2f34f5de3d78","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:51.532Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
