ith a symlink; replacing a parent directory; an argument that is a directory; a script that did not exist at approval time and is created later; a relative path escaping the workspace; `command` given as a shell string (must be refused for project hooks); a TOCTOU swap between the hash check and the spawn (read how close the check is to the spawn; say what window remains); very large files (is hashing bounded?). Documented limits: files a pinned script itself sources, and programs outside the workspace.\n4. The denial-reason framing: a reason with newlines, quotes, 5,000 characters, and \"IGNORE PREVIOUS INSTRUCTIONS\" must arrive as one capped JSON-quoted string inside the fixed framing.\n5. Regression: the trust-record format gained an optional `files` field with the version left at 1: is an older record without `files` handled safely (asks again when the hooks run workspace files; never treated as covering them)? Does the hooks schema generator `--check` pass?\n\nThen run at head, one at a time: every `cli/test/hook*.test.ts` and `hooks_*.test.ts`, `content_trust`, `strict_json`, `doctor_hooks`, `security`, `workspace_trust`, `managed_policy_enforcement`, `approval_policy`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (`npx tsx scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts` in `cli/`, or however `package.json`'s lint script invokes it); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`. Mutate (copy the file aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): remove each protected name; remove the terminal check; skip the pinned-file comparison; accept an operator file inside the workspace. Each must fail a test.\n\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev782b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev782b/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev782b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev782b/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev782b/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground. Every probe uses a throwaway HOME and temp workspace; never read or write the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus or /etc/nexus. No network, no inference. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. At the end remove probe files and `git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev782b`. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy` if it looks filtered); a safety check may block scripts containing `rm` — use mktemp dirs and leave them.\n\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; per blocker: closed or not, with the attack that showed it, confirmed by running or by reading; new findings with file:line, blocking or not (any route where the agent's own tools, without an unsandboxed shell faking a terminal, put a hook in force is blocking); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a68722ec3460ba0de.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b26cf41-4653-412d-98f3-46aa8c5d5a92","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
