{"parentUuid":"5ff02ea0-7fc0-4e7c-9282-27158be7f1b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMy9nv8xidtEqT11nRJX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JXmqR1fmybVqS49pE4gxHb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 782 --body \"**Fixes for the three blockers pushed: head \\`258f72ff\\` (fix commit \\`3f769c90b\\`, plus a merge of the release branch). An independent re-review is running; do not merge before it is posted.**\n\n1. **Self-approval.** \\`extension_trust.json\\` and \\`nexus/hooks.json\\` are protected paths (a project's own \\`.nexus/hooks.json\\` stays writable, by design: editing it only stops the hooks). \\`nexus hooks approve\\` approves only with stdin and stdout on a terminal; \\`--sha256\\` now only says which content is meant. \\`revoke\\` stays non-interactive.\n2. **Workspace = home.** An operator hooks file that lies inside the active workspace is invalid, and every call is denied with guidance.\n3. **Script pinning.** An approval records the SHA-256 of the program and of every argument that is a workspace file, re-checked before each run; a change makes the hooks inactive and names the file. Project hooks must use array commands; a path or symlink leaving the workspace is refused. The trust record gains an optional \\`files\\` field (version stays 1; older approvals of hooks that run workspace files ask again).\n\nAlso: a hook's denial reason now reaches the model as a JSON-quoted string inside a fixed framing sentence; a subagent test was added; \\`docs/HOOKS.md\\` corrected on operation units, \\`!cmd\\`, cancel and deadline, and replaced gate reasons.\n\n**Limit that remains, stated in the docs:** an unsandboxed command in auto mode acts with the operator's rights, so it can fake a terminal or write the trust store with a shell redirect. \\`nexus trust\\` has the same limit. Also not covered: files that a pinned script itself sources.\n\nLocal at this head (Node 24): \\`hooks_self_approval\\` 6/6, \\`hooks_cli\\` 10/10, \\`hooks_project_trust\\` 9/9, \\`hooks_gate_bypass\\` 11/11, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`tsc\\` clean.\" | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #782 fixes pushed (258f72ff); independent re-review running; DO NOT MERGE #782 until its verdict is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 16); do r=$(gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \".[0]|.status+\\\"/\\\"+(.conclusion//\\\"\\\")+\\\"/\\\"+.headSha[0:8]\"); case \"$r\" in completed*) break;; esac; sleep 30; done; echo \"release $r\"'","description":"Post the fix summary on PR 782, log it, and wait for the release CI result","timeout":540000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2668,"cache_read_input_tokens":143179,"output_tokens":1086,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2668,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":143179,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2668},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":8635,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JXmqR1fmybVqS49pE4gxHb":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 782 --body \"**Fixes for the three blockers pushed: head \\`258f72ff\\` (fix commit \\`3f769c90b\\`, plus a merge of the release branch). An independent re-review is running; do not merge before it is posted.**\n\n1. **Self-a